#: docs/birth-stack.md:99
msgid "From requirement to provider"
msgstr "从需求到服务提供方"

#: docs/birth-stack.md:101
msgid ""
"Every layer is satisfied the same way, which is what makes the stack useful "
"rather than just a taxonomy:"
msgstr "每一层都以同样的方式得到满足，这正是让该栈成为实用工具而非仅仅是一套分类法的原因："

#: docs/birth-stack.md:103
msgid ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart LR\n"
"    R[\"Birth requirement<br/><i>the agent needs an inbox</i>\"] --> C[\"Abstract capability<br/><i>send / receive / thread email</i>\"]\n"
"    C --> I[\"Provider interface<br/><i>SMTP+IMAP · JMAP · REST · MCP</i>\"]\n"
"    I --> P1[AgentMail]\n"
"    I --> P2[Fastmail]\n"
"    I --> P3[Resend]\n"
"    I --> P4[self-hosted]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart LR\n"
"    R[\"诞生需求<br/><i>智能体需要一个收件箱</i>\"] --> C[\"抽象能力<br/><i>发送 / 接收 / 邮件会话</i>\"]\n"
"    C --> I[\"提供方接口<br/><i>SMTP+IMAP · JMAP · REST · MCP</i>\"]\n"
"    I --> P1[AgentMail]\n"
"    I --> P2[Fastmail]\n"
"    I --> P3[Resend]\n"
"    I --> P4[自托管]\n"
"```"

#: docs/birth-stack.md:113
msgid ""
"The provider chapters follow this shape: state the requirement, name the "
"interfaces, list the providers. See [Provider model](providers/README.md)."
msgstr "各服务提供方章节遵循这一结构：陈述需求、列出接口、列举提供方。参见[提供方模型](providers/README.md)。"

#: docs/birth-stack.md:115
msgid "Lifecycle"
msgstr "生命周期"

#: docs/birth-stack.md:117
msgid ""
"An agent's stack is not provisioned once and forgotten. Keys rotate, "
"providers change, owners change, agents are retired."
msgstr "智能体的栈并非一次配置后就一劳永逸。密钥会轮换，提供方会更换，所有者会变更，智能体也会退役。"

#: docs/birth-stack.md:119
msgid ""
"```mermaid\n"
"stateDiagram-v2\n"
"    state \"Provisioning\" as Provisioning\n"
"    state \"Active\" as Active\n"
"    state \"Suspended\" as Suspended\n"
"    state \"Migrating\" as Migrating\n"
"    state \"Retired\" as Retired\n"
"    state \"Destroyed\" as Destroyed\n"
"    [*] --> Provisioning : birth begins\n"
"    Provisioning --> Active : Birth Profile complete\n"
"    Active --> Suspended : kill switch / anomaly\n"
"    Suspended --> Active : owner review\n"
"    Active --> Migrating : provider or owner change\n"
"    Migrating --> Active\n"
"    Active --> Retired : purpose ended\n"
"    Suspended --> Retired\n"
"    Retired --> Destroyed : keys revoked, accounts closed, data purged\n"
"    Destroyed --> [*]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```mermaid\n"
"stateDiagram-v2\n"
"    state \"配置中\" as Provisioning\n"
"    state \"活跃\" as Active\n"
"    state \"已暂停\" as Suspended\n"
"    state \"迁移中\" as Migrating\n"
"    state \"已退役\" as Retired\n"
"    state \"已销毁\" as Destroyed\n"
"    [*] --> Provisioning : 诞生开始\n"
"    Provisioning --> Active : 诞生档案完成\n"
"    Active --> Suspended : 紧急停止开关 / 异常\n"
"    Suspended --> Active : 所有者审查\n"
"    Active --> Migrating : 提供方或所有者变更\n"
"    Migrating --> Active\n"
"    Active --> Retired : 使命结束\n"
"    Suspended --> Retired\n"
"    Retired --> Destroyed : 密钥吊销、账户关闭、数据清除\n"
"    Destroyed --> [*]\n"
"```"

#: docs/birth-stack.md:139
msgid ""
"Each transition has its own chapter under [Lifecycle](lifecycle/birth.md)."
msgstr "每个转换在[生命周期](lifecycle/birth.md)下都有专属章节。"

#: docs/birth-stack.md:141
msgid "What the stack is not"
msgstr "该栈不是什么"

#: docs/birth-stack.md:143
msgid ""
"**Not a runtime.** Birthbook does not run agents. LangGraph, the Claude "
"Agent SDK, OpenAI Agents, CrewAI and friends sit _inside_ layer 6."
msgstr ""
"<strong>不是运行时。</strong> Birthbook 不运行智能体。LangGraph、Claude Agent SDK、OpenAI "
"Agents、CrewAI 等都位于第 6 层<em>内部</em>。"

#: docs/birth-stack.md:144
msgid ""
"**Not an identity standard.** DIDs, ERC-8004, A2A Agent Cards, AIMS and "
"agent passports are candidate fillers for layers 1 and 9. Birthbook "
"describes where they fit; it does not compete with them."
msgstr ""
"<strong>不是身份标准。</strong> DID、ERC-8004、A2A Agent Cards、AIMS 和智能体护照是第 1 层和第 9 "
"层的候选实现。Birthbook 描述它们的位置，并不与之竞争。"

#: docs/birth-stack.md:145
msgid ""
"**Not a product catalogue.** Providers are listed because someone has to "
"actually hand the agent an inbox or a wallet, but the layer definitions are "
"the durable part; the provider tables will churn."
msgstr ""
"<strong>不是产品目录。</strong> "
"列出服务提供方是因为总得有人真正把收件箱或钱包交到智能体手上，但层的定义才是持久的部分；提供方表格会不断变动。"

#: docs/glossary.md:3
msgid ""
"Terms the book coins are marked **(Birthbook)**. Everything else is "
"borrowed, with a link to where it is defined."
msgstr "本书自创的术语标注为 <strong>(Birthbook)。</strong>其余术语均为借用，并附有其定义出处的链接。"

#: docs/glossary.md:5
msgid "Birthbook vocabulary"
msgstr "Birthbook 词汇"

#: docs/glossary.md:7
msgid ""
"**Agent Birthbook (Birthbook)** — This knowledge base: a reference "
"architecture for what autonomous agents must be provisioned with."
msgstr ""
"<strong>Agent Birthbook (Birthbook)</strong> —— 本知识库：一套描述自主智能体必须配置哪些资源的参考架构。"

#: docs/glossary.md:9
msgid ""
"**Agent Birth Stack (Birthbook)** — The ten-layer concept model: 1 Identity,"
" 2 Presence, 3 Authentication, 4 Compute, 5 Economic Identity, 6 "
"Capabilities, 7 Memory, 8 Authority, 9 Trust, 10 Governance. See [The Agent "
"Birth Stack](birth-stack.md)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>智能体诞生栈 (Birthbook)</strong> —— 十层概念模型：1 身份、2 在线存在、3 身份验证、4 计算资源、5 "
"经济身份、6 能力、7 记忆、8 权限、9 信任、10 治理。参见[智能体诞生栈](birth-stack.md)。"

#: docs/glossary.md:11
msgid ""
"**Agent Birth Manifest, ABM (Birthbook)** — The machine-readable format for "
"describing an agent's provisioning, one section per layer. File name by "
"convention `birth.yaml`. See [birth.yaml](manifest.md)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>智能体诞生清单，ABM (Birthbook)</strong> —— 用于描述智能体配置的机器可读格式，每层一个部分。按惯例文件名为 "
"`birth.yaml`。参见 [birth.yaml](manifest.md)。"

#: docs/glossary.md:13
msgid ""
"**Birth Profile (Birthbook)** — One agent's manifest; an instance of the "
"ABM."
msgstr "<strong>诞生档案 (Birthbook)</strong> —— 单个智能体的清单；ABM 的一个实例。"

#: docs/glossary.md:15
msgid ""
"**Birth Provider (Birthbook)** — Any party that provisions a resource to an "
"agent: an inbox, a number, a domain, a sandbox, a wallet, a card, a secret "
"store, memory, model access, tools, observability, a legal wrapper. See "
"[Provider model](providers/README.md)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>诞生服务提供方 (Birthbook)</strong> —— "
"向智能体供给资源的任何一方：收件箱、号码、域名、沙箱、钱包、卡片、密钥存储、记忆、模型访问、工具、可观测性、法律包装。参见[提供方模型](providers/README.md)。"

#: docs/glossary.md:17
msgid ""
"**Birth Procedure (Birthbook)** — The provisioning lifecycle: "
"[birth](lifecycle/birth.md), [credential rotation](lifecycle/credential-"
"rotation.md), [migration](lifecycle/migration.md), "
"[death](lifecycle/death.md)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>诞生流程 (Birthbook)</strong> —— "
"配置生命周期：[诞生](lifecycle/birth.md)、[凭证轮换](lifecycle/credential-"
"rotation.md)、[迁移](lifecycle/migration.md)、[死亡](lifecycle/death.md)。"

#: docs/glossary.md:19
msgid ""
"**Existence / Action / Safety bands (Birthbook)** — The grouping of layers "
"1–3, 4–7 and 8–10 respectively."
msgstr ""
"<strong>存在 / 行动 / 安全区带 (Birthbook)</strong> —— 分别对第 1–3 层、第 4–7 层和第 8–10 "
"层的分组。"

#: docs/glossary.md:21
msgid ""
"**Owner** — The natural or legal person responsible for an agent. Every "
"Birth Profile names one. The owner passes KYC, holds the kill switch, and is"
" who a counterparty ultimately has recourse to."
msgstr ""
"<strong>所有者</strong> —— 对智能体负责的自然人或法人。每份诞生档案都指定一位所有者。所有者通过 "
"KYC，持有紧急停止开关，也是交易对手最终可以追索的对象。"

#: docs/glossary.md:23
msgid ""
"**Principal** — The party on whose behalf an agent is acting for a given "
"task. Often the owner, but not always: a customer-service agent acts for the"
" customer within limits set by the owner."
msgstr ""
"<strong>主体</strong> —— "
"在给定任务中智能体代表其行事的一方。通常是所有者，但并非总是如此：客服智能体在所有者设定的限度内为客户行事。"

#: docs/glossary.md:25
msgid "Identity and trust"
msgstr "身份与信任"

#: docs/glossary.md:27
msgid ""
"**DID — Decentralized Identifier** — A URI of the form "
"`did:method:identifier` that resolves to a DID document containing public "
"keys and service endpoints. [W3C DID Core](https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/)."
" Common methods for agents: `did:web` (hosted on the owner's domain), "
"`did:key` (self-describing, no resolution), `did:pkh` (derived from a "
"blockchain address)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>DID —— 去中心化标识符</strong> —— 形如 `did:method:identifier` 的 "
"URI，可解析为包含公钥和服务端点的 DID 文档。[W3C DID Core](https://www.w3.org/TR/did-"
"core/)。智能体常用的方法：`did:web`（托管在所有者的域名上）、`did:key`（自描述，无需解析）、`did:pkh`（从区块链地址派生）。"

#: docs/glossary.md:29
msgid ""
"**VC — Verifiable Credential** — A signed set of claims about a subject, "
"issued by an issuer, checkable by a verifier without contacting the issuer. "
"[W3C VC Data Model 2.0](https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/). In the "
"stack, VCs fill layer 9 Trust."
msgstr ""
"<strong>VC —— 可验证凭证</strong> —— 由签发方签署的关于某主体的一组声明，验证方无需联系签发方即可核验。[W3C VC "
"Data Model 2.0](https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-model-2.0/)。在本栈中，VC 用于第 9 层信任。"

#: docs/glossary.md:31
msgid ""
"**Agent Card** — A JSON document describing an agent's capabilities, "
"endpoints and accepted authentication, published at `/.well-known/agent-"
"card.json` by the [A2A protocol](https://a2a-protocol.org/). ERC-8004 and "
"AIMS define similar but non-identical documents; see [Standards: "
"Identity](standards/identity.md)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>Agent Card</strong> —— 描述智能体的能力、端点和可接受身份验证方式的 JSON 文档，由 [A2A "
"协议](https://a2a-protocol.org/)发布在 `/.well-known/agent-card.json`。ERC-8004 和 "
"AIMS 定义了类似但不完全相同的文档；参见[标准：身份](standards/identity.md)。"

#: docs/glossary.md:33
msgid ""
"**ERC-8004 — Trustless Agents** — Ethereum standard with Identity, "
"Reputation and Validation registries; an agent is an ERC-721 token pointing "
"at a registration file. [EIP-8004](https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-8004)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>ERC-8004 —— Trustless Agents</strong> —— "
"以太坊标准，包含身份、声誉和验证注册表；智能体是一个指向注册文件的 ERC-721 "
"代币。[EIP-8004](https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-8004)。"

#: docs/glossary.md:35
msgid ""
"**AIMS — Agent Identity and Manifest Standard** — Manifest, discovery and "
"verification spec from OpenAttribution so a website can establish which "
"agent is calling it. [Specification](https://github.com/openattribution-"
"org/aims/blob/main/SPECIFICATION.md)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>AIMS —— Agent Identity and Manifest Standard</strong> —— "
"OpenAttribution "
"制定的清单、发现和验证规范，使网站能够确认是哪个智能体在调用它。[规范](https://github.com/openattribution-"
"org/aims/blob/main/SPECIFICATION.md)。"

#: docs/glossary.md:37
msgid ""
"**Agent Passport** — Generic name for a signed document asserting an agent's"
" identity, provenance, and often its authorisation and spend limits. Several"
" unrelated projects use the term; Birthbook does not, because the stack sits"
" _before_ any passport is issued."
msgstr ""
"<strong>智能体护照</strong> —— "
"对一份已签名文档的通称，该文档断言智能体的身份、来源，通常还包括其授权和支出限额。多个互不相关的项目都使用该术语；Birthbook "
"不使用，因为本栈位于任何护照签发<em>之前</em>。"

#: docs/glossary.md:39
msgid ""
"**KYA — Know Your Agent** — Verification of an agent's identity, provenance "
"and permissions before a counterparty transacts with it; the agent-world "
"analogue of KYC. See [AgentFacts KYA](https://agentfacts.org/kya/) and "
"[Standards: Security & Governance](standards/security-and-governance.md)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>KYA —— Know Your Agent</strong> —— "
"在交易对手与智能体交易之前，对其身份、来源和权限进行核验；相当于智能体世界的 KYC。参见 [AgentFacts "
"KYA](https://agentfacts.org/kya/) 和[标准：安全与治理](standards/security-and-"
"governance.md)。"

#: docs/glossary.md:41
msgid ""
"**Attestation** — A signed statement by one party about another; in this "
"book usually the owner attesting to the agent (\"this agent is mine, here is"
" its key\"), or a TEE attesting to the code it runs."
msgstr ""
"<strong>证明</strong> —— "
"一方对另一方作出的签名声明；在本书中通常是所有者对智能体的证明（\"这个智能体是我的，这是它的密钥\"），或 TEE 对其运行代码的证明。"

#: docs/glossary.md:43
msgid ""
"**Provenance** — Where an agent came from: which model, which operator, "
"which code, which owner. A trust signal distinct from identity."
msgstr "<strong>来源</strong> —— 智能体的出处：哪个模型、哪个运营者、哪些代码、哪位所有者。这是一种有别于身份的信任信号。"

#: docs/glossary.md:45
msgid ""
"**Reputation** — Aggregated third-party feedback about an agent's past "
"behaviour, typically in a registry (ERC-8004 Reputation Registry, "
"marketplace ratings)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>声誉</strong> —— 关于智能体过往行为的第三方反馈汇总，通常存于注册表中（ERC-8004 声誉注册表、市场评分）。"

#: docs/glossary.md:47
msgid "Authentication and authority"
msgstr "身份验证与权限"

#: docs/glossary.md:49
msgid ""
"**Authentication vs Identity** — Identity is what the agent _is_ (layer 1); "
"authentication is what it _presents_ to another system to prove it (layer "
"3). An agent has one identity and many credentials."
msgstr ""
"<strong>身份验证 vs 身份</strong> —— 身份是智能体<em>是什么</em>（第 1 "
"层）；身份验证是它向另一系统<em>出示什么</em>来证明这一点（第 3 层）。一个智能体只有一个身份，却有多个凭证。"

#: docs/glossary.md:51
msgid ""
"**Credential (authentication sense)** — An API key, OAuth token, certificate"
" or signature the agent uses to access a service. Not to be confused with "
"Verifiable Credential, which is a trust artifact."
msgstr ""
"<strong>凭证（身份验证意义上）</strong> —— 智能体用于访问服务的 API 密钥、OAuth "
"令牌、证书或签名。切勿与可验证凭证混淆，后者是信任工件。"

#: docs/glossary.md:53
msgid ""
"**Secret store** — The system that holds credentials and hands them to the "
"agent at runtime. A Birth Profile contains `secretRef` pointers, never "
"secret values."
msgstr ""
"<strong>密钥存储</strong> —— 保管凭证并在运行时交给智能体的系统。诞生档案包含 `secretRef` 指针，绝不包含机密值本身。"

#: docs/glossary.md:55
msgid ""
"**OAuth 2.1** — The consolidated OAuth profile (PKCE mandatory, implicit "
"grant removed) that the [MCP authorization "
"spec](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/draft/basic/authorization)"
" builds on."
msgstr ""
"<strong>OAuth 2.1</strong> —— 整合后的 OAuth 配置文件（强制 PKCE，移除隐式授权），[MCP "
"授权规范](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/draft/basic/authorization)以其为基础。"

#: docs/glossary.md:57
msgid ""
"**Token exchange / on-behalf-of** — Swapping one token for another so a "
"downstream service knows both _who_ is acting (`sub`) and _through whom_ "
"(`act`). [RFC 8693](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8693). The agent-"
"specific extension is the IETF [OBO for AI agents "
"draft](https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-oauth-ai-agents-on-behalf-of-"
"user-00.html)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>令牌交换 / 代表模式（on-behalf-of）</strong> —— "
"将一个令牌换为另一个令牌，使下游服务同时知道<em>谁</em>在行事（`sub`）以及<em>通过谁</em>行事（`act`）。[RFC "
"8693](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8693)。针对智能体的扩展是 IETF 的 [OBO for AI "
"agents 草案](https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-oauth-ai-agents-on-behalf-"
"of-user-00.html)。"

#: docs/glossary.md:59
msgid ""
"**Delegation** — A grant from a principal to an agent (or agent to sub-"
"agent) of a bounded authority: scope, expiry, whether it can be re-"
"delegated, and to what depth. Layer 8."
msgstr ""
"<strong>委托授权</strong> —— 主体向智能体（或智能体向子智能体）授予的一项有界权限：范围、有效期、能否再次委托，以及委托深度。第 8"
" 层。"

#: docs/glossary.md:61
msgid ""
"**Attenuation** — The rule that a delegation can only narrow, never widen, "
"the authority of the grantor. Central to capability systems such as "
"[UCAN](https://github.com/ucan-wg/spec) and [ZCAP-"
"LD](https://w3c-ccg.github.io/zcap-spec/)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>权限收窄</strong> —— 委托授权只能收窄、绝不能扩大授予方权限的规则。这是 "
"[UCAN](https://github.com/ucan-wg/spec) 和 [ZCAP-"
"LD](https://w3c-ccg.github.io/zcap-spec/) 等能力系统的核心。"

#: docs/glossary.md:63
msgid ""
"**Approval / human-in-the-loop (HITL)** — An action the agent may not "
"complete without a named human deciding, recorded in "
"`spec.authority.approvals[]`."
msgstr ""
"<strong>审批 / 人在回路 (HITL)</strong> —— 未经指定人员决策，智能体不得完成的操作，记录在 "
"`spec.authority.approvals[]` 中。"

#: docs/glossary.md:65
msgid ""
"**Workload identity** — An identity issued to a running process rather than "
"a person, usually short-lived and automatically rotated. "
"[SPIFFE](https://spiffe.io/) is the reference; the IETF "
"[WIMSE](https://datatracker.ietf.org/wg/wimse/about/) working group is "
"standardising the multi-system case."
msgstr ""
"<strong>工作负载身份</strong> —— "
"签发给运行中进程而非个人的身份，通常短期有效且自动轮换。[SPIFFE](https://spiffe.io/) 是参考实现；IETF 的 "
"[WIMSE](https://datatracker.ietf.org/wg/wimse/about/) 工作组正在为多系统场景制定标准。"

#: docs/glossary.md:67
msgid ""
"**Web Bot Auth** — Signing outbound HTTP requests with [RFC 9421 HTTP "
"Message Signatures](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9421) so a site can "
"verify which agent operator is calling. [Cloudflare's write-"
"up](https://blog.cloudflare.com/web-bot-auth/)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>Web Bot Auth</strong> —— 使用 [RFC 9421 HTTP Message "
"Signatures](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9421) 对出站 HTTP "
"请求进行签名，使网站能够验证是哪个智能体运营者在调用。[Cloudflare "
"的详细介绍](https://blog.cloudflare.com/web-bot-auth/)。"

#: docs/glossary.md:69
msgid "Economy"
msgstr "经济"

#: docs/glossary.md:71
msgid ""
"**Custody** — Who controls a key: `self` (the agent's own host), `owner`, "
"`provider` (a wallet or key service, usually with a policy engine), `tee` "
"(hardware enclave), `mpc` (threshold shares). The single biggest design "
"decision in layers 1 and 5."
msgstr ""
"<strong>托管</strong> — "
"谁控制密钥：`self`（智能体自己的主机）、`owner`（所有者）、`provider`（钱包或密钥服务，通常带有策略引擎）、`tee`（硬件安全区）、`mpc`（门限分片）。这是第"
" 1 层和第 5 层中最重要的设计决策。"

#: docs/glossary.md:73
msgid ""
"**Budget** — Hard spending limits per transaction, per day and per month, "
"enforced outside the agent's own reasoning."
msgstr "<strong>预算</strong> — 按单笔交易、每日和每月设定的硬性支出限额，在智能体自身推理之外强制执行。"

#: docs/glossary.md:75
msgid ""
"**x402** — Paying for an HTTP resource by answering a `402 Payment Required`"
" with a stablecoin payment. [Coinbase "
"x402](https://github.com/coinbase/x402)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>x402</strong> — 通过以稳定币支付响应 `402 Payment Required` 来为 HTTP "
"资源付费。[Coinbase x402](https://github.com/coinbase/x402)。"

#: docs/glossary.md:77
msgid ""
"**AP2 — Agent Payments Protocol** — Google-led protocol in which a user "
"signs _mandates_ (intent, cart) that authorise an agent to complete a "
"purchase. [AP2](https://ap2-protocol.org/)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>AP2 — Agent Payments Protocol</strong> — 由 Google "
"主导的协议，用户签署<em>授权令</em>（意图、购物车），授权智能体完成购买。[AP2](https://ap2-protocol.org/)。"

#: docs/glossary.md:79
msgid ""
"**Agentic token / Shared Payment Token** — A card-network or PSP token bound"
" to a specific agent, merchant and amount so the agent never holds raw card "
"data (Mastercard Agent Pay, Stripe SPT)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>智能体令牌 / Shared Payment Token</strong> — 与特定智能体、商户和金额绑定的卡组织或 PSP "
"令牌，使智能体永远不持有原始卡数据（Mastercard Agent Pay、Stripe SPT）。"

#: docs/glossary.md:81
msgid ""
"**KYC / KYB** — Know Your Customer / Business checks. Passed by the owner or"
" the owner's entity, never by the agent."
msgstr "<strong>KYC / KYB</strong> — 了解你的客户 / 企业审查。由所有者或所有者的实体通过，绝不由智能体通过。"

#: docs/glossary.md:83
msgid "Compute, memory, governance"
msgstr "计算资源、记忆、治理"

#: docs/glossary.md:85
msgid ""
"**Sandbox** — An isolated execution environment for agent code: microVM "
"(Firecracker), container, or process-level."
msgstr "<strong>沙箱</strong> — 智能体代码的隔离执行环境：microVM（Firecracker）、容器或进程级。"

#: docs/glossary.md:87
msgid ""
"**Egress allowlist** — Restricting which hosts a runtime may reach. The "
"cheapest high-value control in layer 4."
msgstr "<strong>出站访问白名单</strong> — 限制运行时可访问的主机。这是第 4 层中成本最低、价值最高的控制手段。"

#: docs/glossary.md:89
msgid ""
"**Memory kinds** — _Working_ (current context), _episodic_ (what happened), "
"_semantic_ (what is known), _files_, _knowledge graph_. Layer 7."
msgstr ""
"<strong>记忆类型</strong> — "
"<em>工作记忆</em>（当前上下文）、<em>情景记忆</em>（发生了什么）、<em>语义记忆</em>（已知的知识）、<em>文件</em>、<em>知识图谱</em>。第"
" 7 层。"

#: docs/glossary.md:91
msgid ""
"**Memory poisoning** — Injecting content into an agent's persistent memory "
"so it misbehaves later. [OWASP "
"ASI06](https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-top-10-for-agentic-"
"applications/)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>记忆投毒</strong> — 向智能体的持久记忆中注入内容，使其在之后行为异常。[OWASP "
"ASI06](https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-top-10-for-agentic-"
"applications/)。"

#: docs/glossary.md:93
msgid ""
"**Audit log** — The append-only record of what the agent did, with which "
"credentials, at what cost. Layer 10's non-negotiable."
msgstr ""
"<strong>审计日志</strong> — 仅可追加的记录，记载智能体做了什么、使用了哪些凭证、花费了多少。这是第 10 层不可妥协的要求。"

#: docs/glossary.md:95
msgid ""
"**Kill switch** — The mechanism and the person that can halt an agent: "
"suspend compute, revoke credentials, freeze wallets, mark registrations "
"revoked. See [Governance](stack/10-governance.md)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>紧急停止开关</strong> — "
"能够停止智能体的机制和人员：暂停计算资源、撤销凭证、冻结钱包、将注册标记为已撤销。参见[治理](stack/10-governance.md)。"

#: docs/glossary.md:97
msgid ""
"**Recovery** — How control over an agent is regained when keys, credentials "
"or the owner are lost."
msgstr "<strong>恢复</strong> — 在密钥、凭证或所有者丢失时，如何重新获得对智能体的控制。"

#: docs/glossary.md:99
msgid ""
"**MCP — Model Context Protocol** — Protocol for connecting agents to tools "
"and data. [modelcontextprotocol.io](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>MCP — Model Context Protocol</strong> — "
"将智能体连接到工具和数据的协议。[modelcontextprotocol.io](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/)。"

#: docs/glossary.md:101
msgid ""
"**A2A — Agent2Agent protocol** — Protocol for agent-to-agent discovery and "
"task exchange. [a2a-protocol.org](https://a2a-protocol.org/)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>A2A — Agent2Agent protocol</strong> — "
"用于智能体之间发现和任务交换的协议。[a2a-protocol.org](https://a2a-protocol.org/)。"

#: docs/glossary.md:103
msgid ""
"**Agent Skills** — Packaged, discoverable instructions and scripts an agent "
"can load (`SKILL.md`). [agentskills.io](https://agentskills.io/)."
msgstr ""
"<strong>Agent Skills</strong> — "
"打包的、可发现的指令和脚本，供智能体加载（`SKILL.md`）。[agentskills.io](https://agentskills.io/)。"

#: docs/stack/01-identity.md:3
msgid ""
"Identity gives the agent a stable answer to two questions: _who is this?_ "
"and _who is responsible for it?_ Concretely that is a name, a resolvable "
"identifier, one or more signing keys, and an owner. Every other layer binds "
"to something in this one: an inbox has an account holder, a wallet has a "
"signer, a delegation has a grantee."
msgstr ""
"身份为智能体提供两个问题的稳定答案：<em>这是谁？</em> 以及 <em>谁对它负责？</em> "
"具体而言，就是一个名称、一个可解析的标识符、一个或多个签名密钥，以及一个所有者。其他每一层都绑定到本层中的某个要素：收件箱有账户持有人，钱包有签名者，委托授权有被授权人。"

#: docs/stack/01-identity.md:5 docs/stack/02-presence.md:5
#: docs/stack/03-authentication.md:5 docs/stack/04-compute.md:5
#: docs/stack/05-economy.md:5 docs/stack/06-capabilities.md:5
#: docs/stack/07-memory.md:5 docs/stack/08-authority.md:5
#: docs/stack/09-trust.md:5 docs/stack/10-governance.md:5
msgid "What the agent needs"
msgstr "智能体需要什么"

#: docs/stack/01-identity.md:7
msgid ""
"Three things get conflated under \"identity\" and it pays to keep them "
"apart. A **name** (`scout`) is for humans and is not unique. An "
"**identifier** (`did:web:agents.example.com:scout`) is unique and resolvable"
" to a document that lists keys and endpoints. A **key** is what the agent "
"actually uses to prove control of the identifier by signing. A name without "
"an identifier cannot be looked up; an identifier without a key cannot be "
"proven; a key without an identifier is just a random public key with no "
"story attached."
msgstr ""
"有三样东西常被混为\"身份\"，将它们区分开是值得的。<strong>名称</strong>（`scout`）供人使用，且不唯一。<strong>标识符</strong>（`did:web:agents.example.com:scout`）是唯一的，可解析为列出密钥和端点的文档。<strong>密钥</strong>是智能体通过签名实际证明对标识符控制权的手段。没有标识符的名称无法查询；没有密钥的标识符无法证明；没有标识符的密钥只是一个没有任何背景的随机公钥。"

#: docs/stack/01-identity.md:9
msgid ""
"The identifier is usually a [W3C DID](https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/). "
"Three methods matter in practice. [`did:key`](https://w3c-ccg.github.io/did-"
"key-spec/) encodes the public key itself: zero infrastructure, but no "
"rotation and nothing to resolve beyond the key. "
"[`did:web`](https://w3c-ccg.github.io/did-method-web/) resolves to a JSON "
"document served from a domain the owner controls: rotatable, discoverable, "
"and it ties the agent to a domain that already carries reputation. "
"[`did:pkh`](https://github.com/w3c-ccg/did-pkh) derives a DID from a "
"blockchain address, which is convenient when the agent's wallet _is_ its "
"identity. Most agents end up with `did:web` or an on-chain registration such"
" as [ERC-8004](https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-8004), plus a key, because"
" those are the two forms other parties can verify without trusting the "
"agent's own word."
msgstr ""
"标识符通常是 [W3C DID](https://www.w3.org/TR/did-"
"core/)。实践中有三种方法值得关注。[`did:key`](https://w3c-ccg.github.io/did-key-spec/) "
"直接编码公钥本身：零基础设施，但无法轮换，除密钥外也无可解析内容。[`did:web`](https://w3c-ccg.github.io/did-"
"method-web/) 解析为由所有者控制的域名提供的 JSON "
"文档：可轮换、可发现，并将智能体与已具备声誉的域名绑定。[`did:pkh`](https://github.com/w3c-ccg/did-pkh) "
"从区块链地址派生 DID，当智能体的钱包<em>就是</em>其身份时非常方便。大多数智能体最终采用 `did:web` 或链上注册（如 "
"[ERC-8004](https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-8004)）加上密钥，因为这是其他方无需信任智能体自述即可验证的两种形式。"

#: docs/stack/01-identity.md:11
msgid ""
"The part that is different from human or service identity is the **owner**. "
"An agent is not a legal person; nothing it signs is binding unless a person "
"or company stands behind it. The owner is therefore not metadata but part of"
" the identity: `metadata.owner` is required in the manifest, and the owner "
"is the entity that KYC checks (see [5. Economic Identity](05-economy.md)), "
"that grants delegations (see [8. Authority](08-authority.md)), and that "
"holds the kill switch (see [10. Governance](10-governance.md)). An agent "
"identity with no owner is unverifiable by design."
msgstr ""
"与人类或服务身份不同的部分是<strong>所有者。</strong>智能体不是法律主体；除非有个人或公司为其背书，否则它签署的任何东西都不具约束力。因此所有者不是元数据，而是身份的一部分：清单中"
" `metadata.owner` 是必填项，所有者是接受 KYC 审查的实体（参见 [5. "
"经济身份](05-economy.md)）、授予委托授权的实体（参见 [8. 权限](08-authority.md)），并且持有紧急停止开关（参见 "
"[10. 治理](10-governance.md)）。没有所有者的智能体身份在设计上就是不可验证的。"

#: docs/stack/01-identity.md:13
msgid ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart LR\n"
"    O[\"Owner<br/><small>did:web:example.com:people:fernando</small>\"] -->|controls| D[\"Agent DID<br/><small>did:web:agents.example.com:scout</small>\"]\n"
"    D -->|lists| K1[\"Signing key<br/><small>Ed25519 · custody: provider</small>\"]\n"
"    D -->|lists| K2[\"Wallet key<br/><small>secp256k1 · custody: mpc</small>\"]\n"
"    D -->|registered in| R1[\"ERC-8004 Identity Registry\"]\n"
"    D -->|published as| R2[\"A2A agent-card.json\"]\n"
"    D -->|declared in| R3[\"AIMS manifest\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart LR\n"
"    O[\"所有者<br/><small>did:web:example.com:people:fernando</small>\"] -->|控制| D[\"智能体 DID<br/><small>did:web:agents.example.com:scout</small>\"]\n"
"    D -->|列出| K1[\"签名密钥<br/><small>Ed25519 · custody: provider</small>\"]\n"
"    D -->|列出| K2[\"钱包密钥<br/><small>secp256k1 · custody: mpc</small>\"]\n"
"    D -->|注册于| R1[\"ERC-8004 Identity Registry\"]\n"
"    D -->|发布为| R2[\"A2A agent-card.json\"]\n"
"    D -->|声明于| R3[\"AIMS manifest\"]\n"
"```"

