#: docs/stack/02-presence.md:3
msgid ""
"Presence is the set of addresses at which the agent can be found and "
"contacted: an email address, a domain, a phone number, and protocol "
"endpoints. An agent with identity but no presence is a name nobody can write"
" to; presence is what makes it a participant rather than a label."
msgstr ""
"在线存在是智能体可被找到和联络的一组地址：电子邮件地址、域名、电话号码和协议端点。有身份但没有在线存在的智能体只是一个无法写信联系的名字；在线存在使其成为参与者而不仅仅是一个标签。"

#: docs/stack/02-presence.md:7
msgid ""
"The reason presence sits this low in the stack is that almost every account "
"on the internet is bootstrapped through it. Sign up for an API, a SaaS tool,"
" a registry or a bank and the flow asks for an email address, sends a "
"verification link, and increasingly asks for a phone number and an SMS code."
" That makes presence a hard dependency of [3. "
"Authentication](03-authentication.md): the agent cannot obtain most "
"credentials until it has an inbox it can read and, often, a number it can "
"receive texts on. Humans never notice this dependency because they already "
"have both."
msgstr ""
"在线存在之所以处于栈中如此低的层级，是因为互联网上几乎每个账户都是通过它引导创建的。注册一个 API、SaaS "
"工具、注册表或银行时，流程会要求提供电子邮件地址、发送验证链接，并且越来越多地要求提供电话号码和短信验证码。这使在线存在成为[3. "
"身份验证](03-authentication.md)的硬性依赖：在拥有一个可读取的收件箱（并且通常还需要一个能接收短信的号码）之前，智能体无法获得大多数凭证。人类从未注意到这一依赖，因为他们本来就两者兼有。"

#: docs/stack/02-presence.md:9
msgid ""
"Agents run into a second problem humans do not: consumer accounts are "
"written for people. Google's [Terms of "
"Service](https://policies.google.com/terms) prohibit creating fake accounts "
"and bypassing sign-up protections, and Gmail sign-up itself demands a phone "
"number and behaviour signals that an automated flow will not pass. The same "
"holds for Outlook.com, iCloud and most free providers. Even when an account "
"is created by hand and handed to the agent, automated access sits in a grey "
"zone and the account can be suspended without appeal, taking every "
"downstream registration with it. The robust answer is an address on a "
"**domain the owner controls**, delivered through an API-first email provider"
" or a self-hosted server: no ToS aimed at humans, no CAPTCHA, full control "
"over DNS, and the same domain doubles as the host of the agent's `did:web` "
"document (see [1. Identity](01-identity.md))."
msgstr ""
"智能体还会遇到人类不会遇到的第二个问题：消费级账户是为人设计的。Google "
"的[服务条款](https://policies.google.com/terms)禁止创建虚假账户和绕过注册保护，而 Gmail "
"注册本身就要求电话号码和行为信号，自动化流程无法通过。Outlook.com、iCloud "
"和大多数免费提供商也是如此。即使账户是手工创建后交给智能体的，自动化访问也处于灰色地带，账户可能被无申诉渠道地停用，并连带失去所有下游注册。稳健的答案是使用<strong>所有者控制的域名</strong>上的地址，通过"
" API 优先的电子邮件提供商或自托管服务器提供：没有面向人类的服务条款、没有 CAPTCHA、对 DNS 有完全控制，同一域名还可兼作智能体 "
"`did:web` 文档的托管主机（参见[1. 身份](01-identity.md)）。"

#: docs/stack/02-presence.md:11
msgid ""
"Phone numbers are the hardest resource in the whole stack. Verification "
"services reject VoIP and virtual numbers as a category, so a Twilio or "
"Telnyx number will pass some OTP checks and fail others, with no way to know"
" in advance. Sending in the US requires [A2P "
"10DLC](https://www.twilio.com/docs/messaging/compliance/a2p-10dlc) brand and"
" campaign registration in the name of a legal entity, which the owner must "
"supply. A real mobile SIM in an eSIM-capable device or a hosted SIM box is "
"often the only thing that works for receiving OTPs, and that is a physical "
"asset the owner has to manage. Plan for phone as an owner-provided resource,"
" not something the agent provisions itself."
msgstr ""
"电话号码是整个栈中最难获取的资源。验证服务会将 VoIP 和虚拟号码整类拒绝，因此 Twilio 或 Telnyx 号码能通过某些 OTP "
"检查却通不过另一些，而且无法提前得知。在美国发送短信需要以法律实体名义完成 [A2P "
"10DLC](https://www.twilio.com/docs/messaging/compliance/a2p-10dlc) "
"品牌和活动注册，这必须由所有者提供。装在支持 eSIM 的设备中的真实移动 SIM 卡或托管 SIM 盒通常是接收 OTP "
"唯一可行的方案，而这是所有者必须管理的实体资产。应将电话规划为所有者提供的资源，而不是智能体自行开通的东西。"

#: docs/stack/02-presence.md:13
msgid ""
"Endpoints are the easy part. An agent that speaks A2A publishes its card at "
"`/.well-known/agent-card.json`; an MCP server publishes its metadata under "
"`/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource` per [RFC 9728](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc9728). Both follow the [RFC 8615](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc8615) well-known URI convention, so a domain plus a static"
" file is enough for other agents and services to discover how to reach it."
msgstr ""
"端点是最容易的部分。使用 A2A 的智能体在 `/.well-known/agent-card.json` 发布其名片；MCP 服务器按 [RFC "
"9728](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9728) 在 `/.well-known/oauth-"
"protected-resource` 下发布其元数据。两者都遵循 [RFC 8615](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc8615) 的 well-known URI "
"约定，因此一个域名加一个静态文件就足以让其他智能体和服务发现如何与其联系。"

