#: docs/stack/03-authentication.md:3
msgid ""
"Authentication is the set of credentials the agent presents to other "
"systems, and the store that holds them. Identity is what the agent _is_; "
"authentication is what it _shows_ to a GitHub API, an MCP server or a "
"payment gateway to be let in. The two are linked by keys but they are not "
"the same thing, and conflating them is how agents end up with a single long-"
"lived secret standing in for everything."
msgstr ""
"身份验证是智能体向其他系统出示的一组凭证，以及保存这些凭证的存储。身份是智能体<em>是</em>什么；身份验证是它向 GitHub API、MCP "
"服务器或支付网关<em>出示</em>以获准进入的东西。二者由密钥关联，但并非同一事物，将两者混为一谈正是智能体最终用一个长期有效的秘密代替一切的根源。"

#: docs/stack/03-authentication.md:7
msgid ""
"An agent accumulates credentials the way a new employee accumulates badges: "
"an OAuth grant for the owner's calendar, an API key for a model gateway, an "
"installation token for a GitHub App, a signing key for outbound HTTP. Each "
"has a service, a type, a set of scopes, a rotation period, and a location. "
"The manifest models exactly that in `spec.authentication.credentials[]`, and"
" the rule that makes the model safe is simple: **the manifest holds "
"references, never secrets**. `secretRef` points into a store; the store is "
"named in `spec.authentication.secretStore`. Without a secret store the "
"agent's secrets live in environment variables, config files and context "
"windows, all of which a prompt injection can read back."
msgstr ""
"智能体积累凭证的方式就像新员工积累工牌：一个用于所有者日历的 OAuth 授权、一个用于模型网关的 API 密钥、一个 GitHub App "
"的安装令牌、一个用于出站 HTTP 的签名密钥。每个凭证都有服务、类型、一组权限范围、轮换周期和存放位置。清单在 "
"`spec.authentication.credentials[]` "
"中对此精确建模，而让这一模型保持安全的规则很简单：<strong>清单只保存引用，绝不保存密钥。</strong>`secretRef` "
"指向一个存储；该存储在 `spec.authentication.secretStore` "
"中命名。没有密钥存储，智能体的密钥就会存在于环境变量、配置文件和上下文窗口中，而提示注入可以把这些内容全部读出。"

#: docs/stack/03-authentication.md:9
msgid ""
"The dominant protocol is OAuth. The [MCP authorization "
"spec](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/draft/basic/authorization)"
" fixes the shape for agent-to-tool access: [OAuth "
"2.1](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-oauth-v2-1/) with PKCE "
"mandatory, [RFC 9728](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9728) Protected "
"Resource Metadata so the client can discover the authorization server from "
"the resource, and [RFC 8707](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8707) "
"resource indicators so a token minted for one MCP server cannot be replayed "
"against another. The human step is the owner's consent screen; after that "
"the agent holds a short-lived access token and a refresh token that the "
"secret store rotates."
msgstr ""
"主导协议是 OAuth。[MCP "
"授权规范](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/draft/basic/authorization)确定了智能体访问工具的形态：强制使用"
" PKCE 的 [OAuth 2.1](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-"
"oauth-v2-1/)、[RFC 9728](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9728) "
"受保护资源元数据（使客户端能从资源发现授权服务器），以及 [RFC 8707](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc8707) 资源指示器（使为某个 MCP "
"服务器签发的令牌无法在另一个服务器上重放）。人工环节是所有者的同意界面；之后智能体持有短期访问令牌和由密钥存储负责轮换的刷新令牌。"

#: docs/stack/03-authentication.md:11
msgid ""
"```mermaid\n"
"sequenceDiagram\n"
"    %% \"i18n\"\n"
"    participant A as Agent\n"
"    participant RS as MCP server (resource)\n"
"    participant AS as Authorization server\n"
"    participant O as Owner\n"
"    A->>RS: request without token\n"
"    RS-->>A: 401 + WWW-Authenticate (RFC 9728 metadata URL)\n"
"    A->>AS: authorization request, PKCE challenge, resource=RS\n"
"    AS->>O: consent screen (scopes, agent name)\n"
"    O-->>AS: approve\n"
"    AS-->>A: authorization code\n"
"    A->>AS: code + PKCE verifier + resource=RS\n"
"    AS-->>A: access token (aud=RS, short-lived) + refresh token\n"
"    A->>RS: request with Bearer token\n"
"    RS-->>A: 200\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```mermaid\n"
"sequenceDiagram\n"
"    %% \"i18n\"\n"
"    participant A as 智能体\n"
"    participant RS as MCP 服务器（资源）\n"
"    participant AS as 授权服务器\n"
"    participant O as 所有者\n"
"    A->>RS: 无令牌请求\n"
"    RS-->>A: 401 + WWW-Authenticate（RFC 9728 元数据 URL）\n"
"    A->>AS: 授权请求、PKCE 质询、resource=RS\n"
"    AS->>O: 同意页面（作用域、智能体名称）\n"
"    O-->>AS: 批准\n"
"    AS-->>A: 授权码\n"
"    A->>AS: 授权码 + PKCE 验证器 + resource=RS\n"
"    AS-->>A: 访问令牌（aud=RS，短期有效）+ 刷新令牌\n"
"    A->>RS: 携带 Bearer 令牌的请求\n"
"    RS-->>A: 200\n"
"```"

#: docs/stack/03-authentication.md:30
msgid ""
"What is specific to agents is the delegation chain. When an agent acts for a"
" user against a downstream API, the downstream API needs to know both _who "
"the subject is_ and _who is acting_. [RFC 8693 token "
"exchange](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8693) does this with the `act` "
"claim: the token says `sub` is the owner and `act` is the agent, and a "
"nested `act` records a sub-agent. Without it, audit logs show the owner "
"doing things the owner never did, and revoking the agent means revoking the "
"owner. The IETF [on-behalf-of draft for AI "
"agents](https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-oauth-ai-agents-on-behalf-of-"
"user-00.html) and the [transaction tokens for agents "
"draft](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-oauth-transaction-tokens-for-"
"agents/) extend the same idea; see [8. Authority](08-authority.md) for the "
"policy side."
msgstr ""
"智能体特有之处在于委托授权链。当智能体代表用户访问下游 API 时，下游 API "
"需要同时知道<em>主体是谁</em>以及<em>谁在执行操作</em>。[RFC 8693 令牌交换](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc8693)通过 `act` 声明实现这一点：令牌声明 `sub` 是所有者，`act` 是智能体，嵌套的 `act`"
" 记录子智能体。没有它，审计日志会显示所有者做了其从未做过的事情，而吊销智能体就意味着吊销所有者。IETF 的[面向 AI 智能体的 on-"
"behalf-of 草案](https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-oauth-ai-agents-on-"
"behalf-of-"
"user-00.html)和[面向智能体的事务令牌草案](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-oauth-"
"transaction-tokens-for-agents/)延伸了同一思路；策略层面见 [8. 权限](08-authority.md)。"

#: docs/stack/03-authentication.md:32
msgid ""
"Two other credential types round out the picture. For outbound requests to "
"sites that have no OAuth relationship with the agent, [RFC 9421 HTTP Message"
" Signatures](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9421) as used by [Web Bot "
"Auth](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-meunier-web-bot-auth-"
"architecture/) let the agent sign each request with a key published from its"
" domain, so a site can tell a named agent from an anonymous scraper. For "
"workload-to-workload calls inside an owner's infrastructure, "
"[SPIFFE](https://spiffe.io/) issues short-lived X.509 or JWT identities per "
"workload with no static secret at all, which is the right fit for the "
"agent's own runtime talking to the owner's internal services."
msgstr ""
"另外两种凭证类型补全了这幅图景。对于向与智能体没有 OAuth 关系的站点发出的出站请求，[Web Bot "
"Auth](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-meunier-web-bot-auth-"
"architecture/) 所使用的 [RFC 9421 HTTP 消息签名](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc9421)让智能体用从其域名发布的密钥对每个请求签名，使站点能够区分具名智能体与匿名爬虫。对于所有者基础设施内部的工作负载间调用，[SPIFFE](https://spiffe.io/)"
" 为每个工作负载签发短期 X.509 或 JWT 身份，完全不需要静态密钥，非常适合智能体自身运行时与所有者内部服务通信的场景。"

