#: docs/stack/05-economy.md:3
msgid ""
"Economic Identity is the agent's ability to hold and move value: wallets, "
"cards, a budget, and the payment protocols it speaks. It turns the agent "
"from a consumer of resources the owner pre-paid into something that can buy "
"what it needs, within limits the owner set in advance."
msgstr ""
"经济身份是智能体持有和转移价值的能力：钱包、卡片、预算，以及它所使用的支付协议。它使智能体从消费所有者预先付费资源的角色，转变为可以在所有者预先设定的限额内自行购买所需资源的角色。"

#: docs/stack/05-economy.md:7
msgid ""
"Nearly everything an agent does costs money at the point of use: model "
"tokens, sandbox minutes, a search API, a dataset, a domain renewal. Today "
"most of that is billed to the owner's card behind an API key, which works "
"until the agent needs something the owner has no account with, or until "
"three agents share one card and nobody can tell who spent what. An "
"instrument of its own, with its own limits, makes spending attributable and "
"boundable. It is also the precondition for agent-to-agent commerce: an agent"
" that sells a service needs somewhere to be paid."
msgstr ""
"智能体所做的几乎每件事都在使用时产生费用：模型 token、沙箱时长、搜索 API、数据集、域名续费。如今这些费用大多通过 API "
"密钥计入所有者的卡片，这种方式在智能体需要所有者没有账户的服务之前、或在三个智能体共用一张卡而无人能分清各自花了多少之前都还行得通。拥有自己的支付工具和限额，能让支出可归因、可约束。这也是智能体间商业往来的前提：出售服务的智能体需要有收款的地方。"

#: docs/stack/05-economy.md:9
msgid ""
"The instruments come in three shapes. **Crypto wallets** hold stablecoins "
"and pay per request over protocols like x402; settlement is instant and "
"amounts can be cents, but the counterparty must accept crypto. **Fiat "
"cards** work everywhere, but issuers require a legal cardholder, chargebacks"
" and KYC apply, and micropayments are impractical. **Stablecoin-backed "
"cards** ([Rain](https://www.rain.xyz), "
"[Crossmint](https://www.crossmint.com)) bridge the two: the agent holds "
"USDC, the card settles in fiat. Most agents end up with a wallet for "
"machine-to-machine payments and a virtual card for the long tail of SaaS."
msgstr ""
"支付工具有三种形态。<strong>加密钱包</strong>持有稳定币，通过 x402 "
"等协议按请求付费；结算即时且金额可以低至几美分，但交易对方必须接受加密货币。<strong>法币卡</strong>处处可用，但发卡方要求有合法持卡人，存在拒付和"
" KYC "
"要求，且微支付不切实际。<strong>稳定币支持的卡片</strong>（[Rain](https://www.rain.xyz)、[Crossmint](https://www.crossmint.com)）连接了两者：智能体持有"
" USDC，卡片以法币结算。大多数智能体最终会同时拥有一个用于机器间支付的钱包和一张用于各种长尾 SaaS 的虚拟卡。"

#: docs/stack/05-economy.md:11
msgid ""
"Custody matters here more than anywhere else, because a leaked wallet key is"
" an irreversible loss. The same five options from [1. "
"Identity](01-identity.md) apply, and the common answer is **provider-held "
"keys behind a policy engine**: [Coinbase CDP Server "
"Wallets](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/server-"
"wallets/v2/introduction/welcome), [Privy](https://privy.io), "
"[Turnkey](https://www.turnkey.com) and [Stripe Issuing for "
"agents](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/agents) let the owner define what "
"the agent may sign or charge and refuse the rest before it reaches the chain"
" or the network. The agent never sees the key; revocation is one API call."
msgstr ""
"托管在这里比在任何其他地方都更重要，因为钱包密钥一旦泄露就是不可逆的损失。[1. "
"身份](01-identity.md)中的五种选项同样适用，而常见答案是<strong>由策略引擎保护的提供方托管密钥：</strong>[Coinbase"
" CDP Server Wallets](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/server-"
"wallets/v2/introduction/welcome)、[Privy](https://privy.io)、[Turnkey](https://www.turnkey.com)"
" 和 [Stripe Issuing for agents](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing/agents) "
"让所有者定义智能体可以签名或扣款的范围，并在请求到达链上或网络之前拒绝其余操作。智能体永远接触不到密钥；撤销只需一次 API 调用。"

#: docs/stack/05-economy.md:13
msgid ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart LR\n"
"    O[Owner] -->|funds and sets policy| W[\"Wallet<br/><small>USDC on Base · custody: provider</small>\"]\n"
"    O -->|issues| C[\"Virtual card<br/><small>Stripe Issuing · merchant controls</small>\"]\n"
"    W --> B[\"Budget<br/><small>perTransaction 2 · perDay 10 · perMonth 150</small>\"]\n"
"    C --> B\n"
"    B -->|within limits| P[\"Payment<br/><small>x402 · card charge</small>\"]\n"
"    B -->|over limit| AP[\"Approval request<br/><small>spec.authority.approvals</small>\"]\n"
"    AP -->|owner approves| P\n"
"    AP -->|denied or timeout| X[Refused]\n"
"    P --> L[\"Audit log<br/><small>spec.governance.auditLog</small>\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart LR\n"
"    O[所有者] -->|注资并设定策略| W[\"钱包<br/><small>USDC on Base · 托管：提供方</small>\"]\n"
"    O -->|签发| C[\"虚拟卡<br/><small>Stripe Issuing · 商户控制</small>\"]\n"
"    W --> B[\"预算<br/><small>perTransaction 2 · perDay 10 · perMonth 150</small>\"]\n"
"    C --> B\n"
"    B -->|限额内| P[\"支付<br/><small>x402 · 卡片扣款</small>\"]\n"
"    B -->|超出限额| AP[\"审批请求<br/><small>spec.authority.approvals</small>\"]\n"
"    AP -->|所有者批准| P\n"
"    AP -->|拒绝或超时| X[已拒绝]\n"
"    P --> L[\"审计日志<br/><small>spec.governance.auditLog</small>\"]\n"
"```"

#: docs/stack/05-economy.md:26
msgid ""
"The budget needs three granularities because they catch different failures. "
"`perTransaction` stops a single absurd purchase. `perDay` stops a loop. "
"`perMonth` is what the owner planned for. Each should be a **hard limit** "
"enforced by the custodian or issuer, not a soft alert the agent is asked to "
"respect; an agent under prompt injection will not respect it, and an alert "
"that arrives after the money is gone is a receipt. Soft alerts still help at"
" 50 and 80 percent so the owner can raise the limit before work stalls. "
"Spending above a hard limit becomes an approval, where [8. "
"Authority](08-authority.md) takes over."
msgstr ""
"预算需要三种粒度，因为它们捕获不同类型的失败。`perTransaction` 阻止一次荒谬的购买。`perDay` 阻止循环失控。`perMonth`"
" "
"是所有者的计划额度。每一项都应是由托管方或发卡方强制执行的<strong>硬性限额，</strong>而不是要求智能体自觉遵守的软性提醒；受到提示注入攻击的智能体不会遵守，而钱花完之后才到达的提醒只是一张收据。软性提醒在"
" 50% 和 80% 时仍然有用，让所有者可以在工作停滞之前提高限额。超过硬性限额的支出会转为审批，由 [8. "
"权限](08-authority.md)接管。"

#: docs/stack/05-economy.md:28
msgid ""
"Payment protocols decide who the agent can pay. "
"[x402](https://www.x402.org/) uses HTTP 402 to negotiate a stablecoin "
"payment per request and is the native fit for API access. Google's "
"[AP2](https://ap2-protocol.org/) adds signed intent and cart mandates so a "
"merchant can prove the user authorised a purchase. On the card side, "
"Stripe's [Shared Payment Tokens](https://docs.stripe.com/agentic-"
"commerce/concepts/shared-payment-tokens) and [Agentic Commerce "
"Protocol](https://github.com/agentic-commerce-protocol/agentic-commerce-"
"protocol), [Mastercard Agent Pay](https://www.mastercard.com/us/en/news-and-"
"trends/stories/2025/agent-pay.html) and [Visa's Trusted Agent "
"Protocol](https://usa.visa.com/about-visa/newsroom/press-"
"releases.releaseId.21618.html) tokenise a card for a specific agent and "
"purchase so the merchant can tell an authorised agent from fraud. List what "
"the agent speaks in `spec.economy.paymentProtocols[]`."
msgstr ""
"支付协议决定智能体可以向谁付款。[x402](https://www.x402.org/) 使用 HTTP 402 为每次请求协商稳定币支付，是 API"
" 访问的原生方案。Google 的 [AP2](https://ap2-protocol.org/) "
"增加了签名的意图和购物车授权，使商家能够证明用户已授权某笔购买。在银行卡方面，Stripe 的 [Shared Payment "
"Tokens](https://docs.stripe.com/agentic-commerce/concepts/shared-payment-"
"tokens) 和 [Agentic Commerce Protocol](https://github.com/agentic-commerce-"
"protocol/agentic-commerce-protocol)、[Mastercard Agent "
"Pay](https://www.mastercard.com/us/en/news-and-trends/stories/2025/agent-"
"pay.html) 以及 [Visa 的 Trusted Agent Protocol](https://usa.visa.com/about-"
"visa/newsroom/press-releases.releaseId.21618.html) "
"会为特定智能体和特定购买将银行卡令牌化，使商家能够区分获授权的智能体与欺诈行为。在 `spec.economy.paymentProtocols[]` "
"中列出智能体支持的协议。"

#: docs/stack/05-economy.md:30
msgid ""
"Two things the agent cannot do for itself. **KYC/KYB**: no issuer or "
"exchange onboards an agent; the owner or the owner's legal entity passes the"
" checks and the agent's wallet or card is a sub-account under that identity "
"(see [Accounts & Legal Entity](../providers/accounts-and-legal-entity.md)). "
"**Tax and accounting**: every payment the agent makes or receives is the "
"owner's income or expense. Each transaction needs an owner, a purpose and a "
"record, which is why the audit log in [10. Governance](10-governance.md) "
"must receive payment events, not just tool calls."
msgstr ""
"有两件事智能体无法自行完成。<strong>KYC/KYB：</strong>没有任何发行方或交易所会为智能体开户；由所有者或所有者的法律实体通过审查，智能体的钱包或银行卡作为该身份下的子账户（参见[账户与法律实体](../providers/accounts-"
"and-legal-"
"entity.md)）<strong>。税务与会计：</strong>智能体的每一笔收付款都是所有者的收入或支出。每笔交易都需要有所有者、用途和记录，这也是为什么[10."
" 治理](10-governance.md)中的审计日志必须接收支付事件，而不仅仅是工具调用。"

#: docs/stack/05-economy.md:36
