#: docs/stack/06-capabilities.md:3
msgid ""
"Capabilities are what the agent can actually do: which models it can call, "
"which tools it can invoke, and which packaged skills it has loaded. "
"Everything below this layer gives the agent a place to stand; this layer "
"gives it hands. It is also the layer where most of the agent-framework "
"ecosystem lives, and where most supply-chain risk enters."
msgstr ""
"能力是智能体实际能做的事情：它可以调用哪些模型、可以调用哪些工具、加载了哪些打包好的技能。此层之下的一切给了智能体立足之地；这一层给了它双手。这也是大多数智能体框架生态所在的层，也是大多数供应链风险进入的层。"

#: docs/stack/06-capabilities.md:7
msgid ""
"**Model access.** An agent needs at least one model it can call, and in "
"practice a primary, a fallback, and often a cheaper model for embeddings or "
"classification. The choice is _direct_ (an API key for one vendor) versus "
"_gateway or router_ (OpenRouter, LiteLLM, Portkey, Vercel or Cloudflare AI "
"Gateway). Gateways matter for agents more than for chat apps because they "
"put a per-key budget, a rate limit, and a fallback chain in front of a "
"process that will otherwise run until the credit card says no. A human "
"notices a $400 bill; an agent in a retry loop does not. Model access is also"
" where [Economic Identity](05-economy.md) and Capabilities meet: the model "
"bill is usually the agent's largest recurring cost."
msgstr ""
"<strong>模型访问。</strong> "
"智能体至少需要一个可调用的模型，实践中通常有一个主模型、一个备用模型，还常常有一个更便宜的模型用于嵌入或分类。选择在于 "
"<em>直连</em>（一个厂商的 API 密钥）还是 <em>网关或路由</em>（OpenRouter、LiteLLM、Portkey、Vercel"
" 或 Cloudflare AI "
"Gateway）。网关对智能体的意义比对聊天应用更大，因为它们在一个否则会一直运行到信用卡说不为止的进程前面加上了按密钥预算、速率限制和回退链。人会注意到"
" 400 "
"美元的账单；处于重试循环中的智能体不会。模型访问也是[经济身份](05-economy.md)与能力交汇之处：模型账单通常是智能体最大的经常性成本。"

#: docs/stack/06-capabilities.md:9
msgid ""
"**Tools.** A tool is anything the agent can call with structured arguments. "
"Four kinds recur: MCP servers (the [Model Context "
"Protocol](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/) has become the default way to "
"expose a tool to any agent), CLIs the agent runs in its sandbox, plain HTTP "
"APIs, and SDKs linked into the agent's own code. Each carries a credential "
"from [Authentication](03-authentication.md) and each is a channel through "
"which untrusted data reaches the model. Agents differ from services here: a "
"service calls the tools its developer wired in; an agent chooses at runtime,"
" from a menu, based on text it read. The menu is therefore a security "
"boundary."
msgstr ""
"<strong>工具。</strong> 工具是智能体可以用结构化参数调用的任何东西。常见的有四类：MCP 服务器（[Model Context "
"Protocol](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/) 已成为向任何智能体暴露工具的默认方式）、智能体在其沙箱中运行的 "
"CLI、普通 HTTP API，以及链接进智能体自身代码的 "
"SDK。每一类都携带来自[身份验证](03-authentication.md)的凭证，且每一类都是不受信任数据到达模型的通道。智能体在此与服务不同：服务调用其开发者预先接入的工具；智能体在运行时根据其读到的文本从菜单中选择。因此，这份菜单是一道安全边界。"

#: docs/stack/06-capabilities.md:11
msgid ""
"**Skills.** Skills are the emerging unit of packaged procedural knowledge: a"
" folder with a `SKILL.md` (name, description, instructions) plus optional "
"scripts and references, loaded on demand. Anthropic released the format as "
"the open [Agent Skills](https://agentskills.io/) specification and it is now"
" read by many agent products. A skill is not a tool; it is instructions "
"_about_ using tools, which means it is executable prose and should be "
"reviewed as code."
msgstr ""
"<strong>技能。</strong> 技能是新兴的打包程序性知识单元：一个包含 "
"`SKILL.md`（名称、描述、指令）以及可选脚本和参考资料的文件夹，按需加载。Anthropic 已将该格式作为开放的 [Agent "
"Skills](https://agentskills.io/) 规范发布，现已被许多智能体产品支持读取。技能不是工具；它是 <em>关于</em> "
"使用工具的指令，这意味着它是可执行的文字，应当像代码一样接受评审。"

#: docs/stack/06-capabilities.md:13
msgid ""
"**Frameworks live here, not above.** LangGraph, the Claude Agent SDK, the "
"OpenAI Agents SDK, CrewAI and similar orchestrators are ways of arranging "
"models, tools and skills into a loop. They are fillers for this layer. "
"Birthbook does not choose one; it asks what the loop has been given."
msgstr ""
"<strong>框架位于这一层，而非其上。</strong> LangGraph、Claude Agent SDK、OpenAI Agents "
"SDK、CrewAI 及类似的编排器是将模型、工具和技能组织成循环的方式。它们是这一层的填充物。诞生手册不选择其中之一；它只问这个循环被赋予了什么。"

