#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:3
msgid ""
"Governance is how the owner watches, limits, recovers and, if necessary, "
"stops the agent. It is the top layer because it has to reach into all the "
"others: the audit log records what Capabilities did, the limits cap Economic"
" Identity and Compute, the kill switch revokes Authentication and Authority "
"and marks Trust registries, and recovery restores Identity. It is the last "
"layer provisioned."
msgstr ""
"治理是所有者监视、限制、恢复以及在必要时停止智能体的方式。它位于最顶层，因为它必须触及所有其他层：审计日志记录能力层的行为，各项限制约束经济身份与计算资源，紧急停止开关撤销身份验证与权限并在信任注册表中做出标记，恢复机制则还原身份。它是最后一个被配置的层。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:7
msgid ""
"**An audit log, non-negotiable.** Every model call, tool call, payment, "
"credential use and approval decision goes to a store the agent cannot edit. "
"This is the one governance control that applies even to the smallest "
"internal script (see [Minimum viable birth](../birth-stack.md#minimum-"
"viable-birth)). The practical shape is a trace: OpenTelemetry's GenAI "
"semantic conventions define spans for model and agent operations, and "
"tracing products (Langfuse, LangSmith, Arize Phoenix, Braintrust) consume "
"them. An agent's [memory](07-memory.md) is writable by the agent, so it is "
"not evidence. The log is."
msgstr ""
"<strong>审计日志，没有商量余地。</strong> "
"每次模型调用、工具调用、支付、凭证使用和审批决策都写入智能体无法编辑的存储。这是唯一一项连最小的内部脚本也必须遵守的治理控制（参见[最小可行诞生](../birth-"
"stack.md#minimum-viable-birth)）。其实际形态是追踪（trace）：OpenTelemetry 的 GenAI "
"语义约定为模型与智能体操作定义了 span，追踪产品（Langfuse、LangSmith、Arize "
"Phoenix、Braintrust）可以消费它们。智能体的[记忆](07-memory.md)可被智能体写入，因此不能作为证据。日志才是。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:9
msgid ""
"**Limits.** Four kinds, all enforced outside the model. _Spend_: per-"
"transaction, per-day, per-month, enforced by the wallet or card provider "
"([Economic Identity](05-economy.md)). _Rate_: calls per minute to models and"
" tools, enforced at the gateway. _Runtime_: hours per day, enforced by the "
"[Compute](04-compute.md) scheduler. _Blast radius_: which systems the agent "
"can touch at all, enforced by network egress allowlists and tool allowlists "
"([Capabilities](06-capabilities.md)). A limit the model is asked to respect "
"is a suggestion."
msgstr ""
"<strong>限制。</strong> "
"四种类型，全部在模型之外强制执行。<em>支出</em>：按单笔交易、按天、按月，由钱包或卡服务商强制执行（[经济身份](05-economy.md)）。<em>速率</em>：对模型和工具的每分钟调用次数，在网关处强制执行。<em>运行时长</em>：每天运行小时数，由[计算资源](04-compute.md)调度器强制执行。<em>影响范围</em>：智能体究竟能触及哪些系统，由网络出站访问白名单和工具白名单强制执行（[能力](06-capabilities.md)）。要求模型自觉遵守的限制只是一种建议。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:11
msgid ""
"**A kill switch, and someone who holds it.** Stopping an agent is not one "
"action; it is four, and a partial stop leaves a running process with money, "
"or a dead process with live credentials. The controller must be a named "
"party (the owner, an on-call role, or a governance service) with pre-"
"provisioned access to each arm, and the switch must work when the agent's "
"own infrastructure is compromised, which means it cannot run on the agent's "
"runtime."
msgstr ""
"<strong>紧急停止开关，以及持有它的人。</strong> "
"停止一个智能体不是一个动作，而是四个；部分停止会留下一个仍持有资金的运行中进程，或一个凭证仍然有效的已死进程。控制者必须是明确指定的一方（所有者、值班角色或治理服务），并预先具备对每条控制路径的访问权限；而且即使智能体自身的基础设施被攻陷，开关也必须能生效，这意味着它不能运行在智能体的运行时之上。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:13
msgid ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart TB\n"
"    K[\"Kill switch<br/><small>controller: owner · trigger: manual / anomaly / limit breach</small>\"]\n"
"    K --> C[\"Compute<br/><small>suspend runtime, revoke sandbox token</small>\"]\n"
"    K --> A[\"Authentication<br/><small>revoke OAuth grants, rotate API keys, disable secret-store path</small>\"]\n"
"    K --> W[\"Economic Identity<br/><small>freeze wallet policy, cancel cards</small>\"]\n"
"    K --> T[\"Trust registries<br/><small>mark revoked: status list, ERC-8004, agent card</small>\"]\n"
"    K --> L[\"Audit log<br/><small>record who pulled it and why</small>\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart TB\n"
"    K[\"紧急停止开关<br/><small>控制者：所有者 · 触发：手动 / 异常 / 超限</small>\"]\n"
"    K --> C[\"计算资源<br/><small>暂停运行时，撤销沙箱令牌</small>\"]\n"
"    K --> A[\"身份验证<br/><small>撤销 OAuth 授权，轮换 API 密钥，禁用密钥存储路径</small>\"]\n"
"    K --> W[\"经济身份<br/><small>冻结钱包策略，注销卡片</small>\"]\n"
"    K --> T[\"信任注册表<br/><small>标记为已撤销：状态列表、ERC-8004、智能体名片</small>\"]\n"
"    K --> L[\"审计日志<br/><small>记录是谁触发以及原因</small>\"]\n"
"```"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:23
msgid ""
"**Recovery.** Three losses to plan for. _Lost keys_: the agent's signing key"
" is gone or compromised; recovery means a rotation path where a new key is "
"bound to the same identity by the owner ([Identity](01-identity.md), "
"[Credential Rotation](../lifecycle/credential-rotation.md)). _Lost owner_: "
"the person leaves, dies, or the company folds; recovery means a documented "
"successor and a second custody share. _Provider outage_: the runtime, "
"gateway or memory provider is down or gone; recovery means exports exist and"
" the [Migration](../lifecycle/migration.md) procedure has been rehearsed."
msgstr ""
"<strong>恢复。</strong> "
"需要为三类丢失做好规划。<em>密钥丢失</em>：智能体的签名密钥丢失或被泄露；恢复意味着有一条轮换路径，由所有者将新密钥绑定到同一身份（[身份](01-identity.md)、[凭证轮换](../lifecycle/credential-"
"rotation.md)）。<em>所有者丢失</em>：此人离职、去世或公司倒闭；恢复意味着有书面记录的继任者和第二份托管份额。<em>服务提供方中断</em>：运行时、网关或记忆提供方宕机或消失；恢复意味着导出已存在，且[迁移](../lifecycle/migration.md)流程已经过演练。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:25
msgid ""
"**Review cadence.** Delegations accumulate, limits drift, credentials "
"outlive their reason. A recurring human review of the whole Birth Profile "
"against what the agent actually did is how scope creep gets reversed. "
"Monthly is a reasonable default for an agent that spends money; quarterly "
"for one that only reads."
msgstr ""
"<strong>审查节奏。</strong> "
"委托授权不断累积，限额逐渐漂移，凭证的存续超出其存在理由。定期由人工将整份诞生档案与智能体的实际行为进行对照审查，才能逆转权限蔓延。对于会花钱的智能体，每月一次是合理的默认值；对于只读的智能体，每季度一次即可。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:31
msgid "Audit log"
msgstr "审计日志"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:31
msgid "Append-only file the agent cannot write to"
msgstr "智能体无法写入的仅追加文件"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:31
msgid ""
"OTel GenAI traces to a hosted tracing system, retention set, tamper-evident"
msgstr "将 OTel GenAI 追踪数据发送到托管的追踪系统，设置保留期限，具备防篡改能力"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:32
