msgid ""
"`reviewCadence` on the calendar, with the log and the manifest side by side"
msgstr "将 `reviewCadence` 排入日历，日志与清单并排对照"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:36
msgid "Anomaly detection"
msgstr "异常检测"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:36
msgid ""
"Alerts on spend spikes, unusual tools, failed approvals, new counterparties"
msgstr "针对支出激增、异常工具、审批失败和新交易对手发出告警"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:40
msgid ""
"Depends on every layer having a control point: [3. "
"Authentication](03-authentication.md) (revocable credentials), [4. "
"Compute](04-compute.md) (suspendable runtime), [5. Economic "
"Identity](05-economy.md) (policy-enforced wallet), [8. "
"Authority](08-authority.md) (revocable delegations), [9. Trust](09-trust.md)"
" (revocable credentials and registry flags)."
msgstr ""
"依赖于每一层都有控制点：[3. 身份验证](03-authentication.md)（可吊销的凭证）、[4. "
"计算资源](04-compute.md)（可暂停的运行时）、[5. 经济身份](05-economy.md)（受策略约束的钱包）、[8. "
"权限](08-authority.md)（可撤销的委托授权）、[9. 信任](09-trust.md)（可吊销的凭证和注册表标记）。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:41
msgid ""
"Enables the [lifecycle](../lifecycle/death.md): Suspended, Retired and "
"Destroyed are governance actions."
msgstr "支撑[生命周期](../lifecycle/death.md)：暂停、退役和销毁都是治理动作。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:42
msgid ""
"Makes [Trust](09-trust.md) credible: a counterparty's KYA check is stronger "
"when the operator can show governance is in place."
msgstr "让[信任](09-trust.md)更可信：当运营方能证明治理已到位时，交易对手的 KYA 检查会更有分量。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:46
msgid ""
"**Kill switch on the agent's own infrastructure.** If the switch is a tool "
"the agent calls, a hijacked agent will not call it. Hold it outside."
msgstr ""
"<strong>紧急停止开关不能放在智能体自身的基础设施上。</strong> "
"如果开关是智能体调用的一个工具，被劫持的智能体就不会去调用它。请将其置于外部。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:47
msgid ""
"**Partial kill.** Runtime suspended, credentials still valid; a copy resumes"
" elsewhere. Rogue-agent scenarios ([OWASP "
"ASI10](https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-top-10-for-agentic-"
"applications/)) are mostly incomplete kills."
msgstr ""
"<strong>部分停止。</strong> 运行时被暂停，但凭证仍然有效；副本在别处恢复运行。失控智能体场景（[OWASP "
"ASI10](https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-top-10-for-agentic-"
"applications/)）大多源于不彻底的停止。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:48
msgid ""
"**Log the agent can edit.** Traces written to the agent's own storage are "
"memory, not audit. Ship them out."
msgstr "<strong>智能体可编辑的日志。</strong> 写入智能体自身存储的追踪数据是记忆，而非审计。请将其外送。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:49
msgid ""
"**Single owner, single key, single share.** Recovery that depends on one "
"person's laptop is not recovery. Two shares, two people."
msgstr "<strong>单一所有者、单一密钥、单一份额。</strong> 依赖一个人笔记本电脑的恢复不是真正的恢复。至少两份份额、两个人。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:50
msgid ""
"**Cascading failures (ASI08).** One agent's kill triggers retries in others."
" Coordinate limits across a fleet; the kill switch should be able to stop "
"dependants too."
msgstr ""
"<strong>级联故障（ASI08）。</strong> "
"一个智能体被终止会触发其他智能体的重试。需在整个集群范围内协调限额；紧急停止开关应能同时停止依赖方。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:51
msgid ""
"**Personal data in traces.** The audit log often contains more personal data"
" than memory does. Apply retention and access control to it as well."
msgstr "<strong>追踪记录中的个人数据。</strong> 审计日志中包含的个人数据往往比记忆中更多。同样需对其应用保留策略和访问控制。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:55
msgid ""
"[Security & Governance](../standards/security-and-governance.md) - OWASP Top"
" 10 for Agentic Applications (ASI08, ASI10); [OpenTelemetry GenAI semantic "
"conventions](https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-genai); "
"NIST and CSA guidance."
msgstr ""
"[安全与治理](../standards/security-and-governance.md) - OWASP "
"智能体应用十大风险（ASI08、ASI10）；[OpenTelemetry GenAI 语义约定](https://github.com/open-"
"telemetry/semantic-conventions-genai)；NIST 和 CSA 指南。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:56
msgid ""
"Regulatory touchpoints, kept brief: [EU AI Act Article "
"12](https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/12/) requires high-risk "
"systems to automatically record events over their lifetime; [NIST AI "
"800-4](https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.AI.800-4) catalogues post-deployment "
"monitoring challenges and expects a \"monitorability tax\"; Singapore's "
"[IMDA Model AI Governance Framework for Agentic "
"AI](https://www.imda.gov.sg/-/media/imda/files/about/emerging-tech-and-"
"research/artificial-intelligence/mgf-for-agentic-ai.pdf) sets out levels of "
"human involvement and agent boundaries. None mandate a specific mechanism; "
"all assume a log and a stop button exist."
msgstr ""
"监管相关要点，简要列出：[EU AI Act 第 12 "
"条](https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/12/)要求高风险系统在其整个生命周期内自动记录事件；[NIST"
" AI 800-4](https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.AI.800-4) "
"归纳了部署后监控的挑战，并预期存在\"可监控性成本\"；新加坡的 [IMDA 智能体 AI "
"治理模型框架](https://www.imda.gov.sg/-/media/imda/files/about/emerging-tech-and-"
"research/artificial-intelligence/mgf-for-agentic-"
"ai.pdf)规定了人类参与的层级和智能体边界。它们都未强制要求特定机制；但都默认存在日志和停止按钮。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:57
msgid ""
"[Authentication & Delegation](../standards/auth-and-delegation.md) - "
"revocation semantics of OAuth grants and short-lived tokens."
msgstr ""
"[身份验证与委托授权](../standards/auth-and-delegation.md) - OAuth 授权与短期令牌的撤销语义。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:61
msgid ""
"[Observability & Human-in-the-loop](../providers/observability-and-hitl.md) "
"- Langfuse, LangSmith, Arize Phoenix, Braintrust, AgentOps; OpenMeter for "
"metering; HumanLayer and gotoHuman for approvals; guardrail products."
msgstr ""
"[可观测性与人在回路](../providers/observability-and-hitl.md) - "
"Langfuse、LangSmith、Arize Phoenix、Braintrust、AgentOps；用于计量的 OpenMeter；用于审批的 "
"HumanLayer 和 gotoHuman；护栏产品。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:62
msgid ""
"[Models & Skills](../providers/models-and-skills.md) - gateways with per-key"
" budgets and rate limits."
msgstr "[模型与技能](../providers/models-and-skills.md) - 具备按密钥预算和速率限制的网关。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:63
msgid ""
"[Wallets & Keys](../providers/wallets.md) and [Payments & "
"Cards](../providers/payments-and-cards.md) - policy engines, freeze and "
"cancel controls."
msgstr ""
"[钱包与密钥](../providers/wallets.md) 及 [支付与卡片](../providers/payments-and-"
"cards.md) - 策略引擎、冻结与取消控制。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:64
msgid ""
"[Compute & Browsers](../providers/compute-and-browsers.md) - runtimes that "
"can be suspended and time-boxed."
msgstr "[计算资源与浏览器](../providers/compute-and-browsers.md) - 可暂停并限时运行的运行时。"

#: docs/stack/10-governance.md:68
msgid ""
"`spec.governance.auditLog` names where traces go; "
"`spec.governance.killSwitch` names the `controller` and the `mechanism` "
"(`revoke-keys | suspend-runtime | freeze-wallet | all`); "
"`spec.governance.limits` is free-form for anything not already in "
"[`spec.economy.budget`](05-economy.md); `spec.governance.recovery` describes"
" how control is regained; `spec.governance.reviewCadence` is an ISO 8601 "
"duration."
msgstr ""
"`spec.governance.auditLog` 指明追踪数据的去向；`spec.governance.killSwitch` 指明 "
"`controller` 和 `mechanism`（`revoke-keys | suspend-runtime | freeze-wallet | "
"all`）；`spec.governance.limits` 为自由格式，用于 "
"[`spec.economy.budget`](05-economy.md) 中尚未涵盖的内容；`spec.governance.recovery` "
"描述如何重新获得控制权；`spec.governance.reviewCadence` 为 ISO 8601 时长。"

