#: docs/standards/auth-and-delegation.md:1
msgid "Authentication & delegation standards"
msgstr "身份验证与委托授权标准"

#: docs/standards/auth-and-delegation.md:3
msgid ""
"Layer 3 is about the credentials an agent presents to other systems; layer 8"
" is about whether it was allowed to. The standards here cover both ends: how"
" an agent obtains a token for a resource (MCP Authorization, OAuth 2.1, "
"GNAP), how a token can say _this agent acts for that user_ (RFC 8693 Token "
"Exchange, the on-behalf-of and transaction-token drafts), how a workload "
"proves what it is without a user at all (SPIFFE, WIMSE, Web Bot Auth), and "
"the capability-based alternative where the authorization _is_ the credential"
" (UCAN, ZCAP). Nearly everything is OAuth-shaped; the open question is how "
"to express a chain human → agent → sub-agent → tool in a way resource "
"servers can verify."
msgstr ""
"第 3 层关注智能体向其他系统出示的凭证；第 8 层关注它是否被允许这样做。这里的标准覆盖两端：智能体如何获取资源的令牌（MCP "
"Authorization、OAuth 2.1、GNAP），令牌如何表达 <em>此智能体代表该用户行事</em>（RFC 8693 Token "
"Exchange、on-behalf-of 与 transaction-token "
"草案），工作负载如何在完全没有用户的情况下证明自己的身份（SPIFFE、WIMSE、Web Bot Auth），以及基于能力的替代方案——授权本身 "
"<em>就是</em> 凭证（UCAN、ZCAP）。几乎所有方案都是 OAuth 形态的；悬而未决的问题是如何以资源服务器可验证的方式表达 人 → "
"智能体 → 子智能体 → 工具 这条链。"

