#: docs/standards/security-and-governance.md:42
msgid ""
"The February 2025 threat model (T1–T15: memory poisoning, tool misuse, "
"privilege compromise, resource overload, cascading hallucination, intent "
"breaking, misaligned behaviour, repudiation, identity spoofing, overwhelming"
" HITL, unexpected RCE, agent communication poisoning, rogue agents, human "
"attacks on multi-agent systems, human manipulation) from which the Top 10 "
"was distilled. Use it when you need the finer-grained mitigations behind "
"each ASI entry."
msgstr ""
"2025 年 2 月的威胁模型（T1–T15：记忆投毒、工具滥用、特权失陷、资源过载、级联幻觉、意图破坏、行为失准、抵赖、身份冒充、压垮 HITL、意外"
" RCE、智能体通信投毒、失控智能体、针对多智能体系统的人为攻击、人为操纵），Top 10 正是从中提炼而来。当你需要每个 ASI "
"条目背后更细粒度的缓解措施时可参考它。"

#: docs/standards/security-and-governance.md:45
msgid ""
"August 2025 paper arguing that OAuth-style static roles do not fit agents "
"and proposing an IAM built on DIDs, Verifiable Credentials, zero-trust per-"
"request policy and fine-grained delegation. It is the clearest statement of "
"why layers 1, 3 and 8 are separate. Guidance, not a spec."
msgstr ""
"2025 年 8 月的论文，主张 OAuth 式的静态角色不适用于智能体，并提出一种基于 DID、可验证凭证（Verifiable "
"Credentials）、零信任逐请求策略和细粒度委托授权的 IAM。它是对第 1、3、8 层为何相互独立的最清晰阐述。属于指导性文档，而非规范。"

#: docs/standards/security-and-governance.md:48
msgid ""
"The Center for AI Standards and Innovation programme convening industry on "
"agent identity, interoperability and security protocols. No normative output"
" yet; it is where US-government-recognised agent standards are likely to be "
"blessed."
msgstr ""
"Center for AI Standards and Innovation "
"的计划，召集业界共同探讨智能体身份、互操作性和安全协议。尚无规范性成果；它是美国政府认可的智能体标准最有可能获得认定之处。"

#: docs/standards/security-and-governance.md:51
msgid ""
"March 2026 report cataloguing what post-deployment monitoring of AI systems "
"requires and where practice falls short, based on three workshops and a "
"literature review. It is the reference for what `spec.governance.auditLog` "
"and `reviewCadence` should be able to answer. Not agent-specific but "
"directly applicable."
msgstr ""
"2026 年 3 月的报告，基于三次研讨会和文献综述，梳理了 AI 系统部署后监控的要求以及现有实践的不足。它是 "
"`spec.governance.auditLog` 和 `reviewCadence` "
"应当能够回答哪些问题的参考依据。并非专门针对智能体，但可直接适用。"

#: docs/standards/security-and-governance.md:54
msgid ""
"Draft CSF 2.0 Community Profile covering cybersecurity _of_ AI systems, AI-"
"enabled attacks and AI-enabled defence. Map your Governance layer to its "
"Govern/Identify/Protect/Detect/Respond/Recover outcomes if you need to show "
"CSF alignment."
msgstr ""
"CSF 2.0 社区档案草案，涵盖 AI 系统<em>自身</em>的网络安全、AI 赋能的攻击和 AI 赋能的防御。若需展示与 CSF "
"的对齐，可将你的治理层映射到其 Govern/Identify/Protect/Detect/Respond/Recover 结果。"

#: docs/standards/security-and-governance.md:56
msgid "Know Your Agent"
msgstr "了解你的智能体（Know Your Agent）"

#: docs/standards/security-and-governance.md:57
msgid ""
"Two things share the name. **AgentFacts KYA** (from the NANDA orbit) "
"proposes signed, verifiable agent metadata (identity, capabilities, "
"compliance, provenance) checked before an agent is admitted, KYC-style. "
"**Skyfire's `kya` token** is a shipping JWT a seller verifies to learn a "
"paying agent's verified identity. Both fill `spec.trust.kya`; see "
"[Trust](../stack/09-trust.md) and [Payments](payments.md)."
msgstr ""
"有两个事物共用此名称。<strong>AgentFacts KYA</strong>（源自 NANDA "
"生态）提出经签名、可验证的智能体元数据（身份、能力、合规、来源），在智能体获准接入前进行核验，类似 KYC。**Skyfire 的 `kya` "
"令牌**是已投入使用的 JWT，卖方通过验证它来获知付费智能体的已验证身份。二者都可填入 "
"`spec.trust.kya`；参见[信任](../stack/09-trust.md)和[支付](payments.md)。"

#: docs/standards/security-and-governance.md:60
msgid ""
"Launched January 2026, updated to v1.5 in May 2026. Four dimensions: bound "
"risks up front, keep humans accountable, apply lifecycle technical controls "
"(baseline testing, allow-listed services), enable end-user responsibility. "
"The most concrete government checklist for agent deployers; short and "
"readable."
msgstr ""
"于 2026 年 1 月发布，2026 年 5 月更新至 "
"v1.5。四个维度：预先界定风险边界、保持人类问责、实施生命周期技术控制（基线测试、白名单服务）、落实最终用户责任。是面向智能体部署方的最具体的政府检查清单；简短易读。"

#: docs/standards/security-and-governance.md:63
msgid ""
"Regulation (EU) 2024/1689. Touchpoints for agents: general-purpose model "
"obligations on the model provider (layer 6), transparency duties when an "
"agent interacts with people (layer 2/9), high-risk obligations if the "
"agent's _use case_ falls in Annex III (layers 8 and 10: human oversight, "
"logging, record-keeping). Whether an autonomous agent is a \"deployer\" or "
"part of a \"system\" is unsettled; log everything and keep a human principal"
" named in `spec.authority.principal`."
msgstr ""
"法规 (EU) 2024/1689。与智能体相关的要点：模型提供方承担通用模型义务（第 6 层）、智能体与人交互时的透明度义务（第 2/9 "
"层）、若智能体的<em>使用场景</em>落入附件 III 则适用高风险义务（第 8 和第 10 "
"层：人类监督、日志记录、记录保存）。自主智能体属于\"部署者\"还是\"系统\"的一部分尚无定论；请记录一切，并在 "
"`spec.authority.principal` 中始终指定一位人类主体。"

#: docs/standards/security-and-governance.md:66
msgid ""
"Engineering guidance (December 2024): prefer simple composable workflows, "
"add autonomy only where needed, keep tool interfaces well-documented, and "
"stop at checkpoints for human review. Its \"start simple\" advice is the "
"practitioner's version of least agency and shapes what a minimum viable "
"[Capabilities](../stack/06-capabilities.md) layer looks like."
msgstr ""
"工程指南（2024 年 12 "
"月）：优先采用简单可组合的工作流，仅在必要处增加自主性，保持工具接口文档完善，并在检查点停下来接受人工审查。其\"从简单开始\"的建议是最小自主性原则的实践者版本，并塑造了最小可行[能力](../stack/06-capabilities.md)层的形态。"

#: docs/standards/security-and-governance.md:70
msgid ""
"OWASP tells you what to defend against; CSA and the IETF/OAuth work in "
"[Authentication & Delegation](auth-and-delegation.md) tell you how to build "
"the identity and permission controls; NIST and IMDA tell you what monitoring"
" and accountability a regulator or auditor will expect; KYA schemes let a "
"counterparty check you did it. In manifest terms: ASI03/ASI07 controls land "
"in `spec.authentication` and `spec.trust`; ASI01/02/09 in `spec.authority` "
"(scopes and approvals); ASI04/05/06 in `spec.capabilities`, "
"`spec.compute.isolation` and `spec.memory`; ASI08/10 in `spec.governance` "
"(limits, `killSwitch`, `recovery`). The unsolved parts are shared with the "
"other chapters: revoking a compromised agent's credentials across many "
"providers at once, and standardised evidence that a kill switch actually "
"works."
msgstr ""
"OWASP 告诉你要防御什么；CSA 以及[身份验证与委托授权](auth-and-delegation.md)中的 IETF/OAuth "
"工作告诉你如何构建身份与权限控制；NIST 和 IMDA 告诉你监管机构或审计方将期望怎样的监控与问责；KYA "
"机制让交易对手可以核验你确实做到了。用清单术语来说：ASI03/ASI07 控制落在 `spec.authentication` 和 "
"`spec.trust`；ASI01/02/09 落在 `spec.authority`（作用域与审批）；ASI04/05/06 落在 "
"`spec.capabilities`、`spec.compute.isolation` 和 `spec.memory`；ASI08/10 落在 "
"`spec.governance`（限制、`killSwitch`、`recovery`）。尚未解决的部分与其他章节相同：如何跨多个提供方同时撤销被入侵智能体的凭证，以及如何提供标准化证据证明紧急停止开关确实有效。"

#: docs/standards/security-and-governance.md:74
msgid ""
"Stack: [3. Authentication](../stack/03-authentication.md) · [4. "
"Compute](../stack/04-compute.md) · [6. "
"Capabilities](../stack/06-capabilities.md) · [7. "
"Memory](../stack/07-memory.md) · [8. Authority](../stack/08-authority.md) · "
"[9. Trust](../stack/09-trust.md) · [10. "
"Governance](../stack/10-governance.md)"
msgstr ""
"栈：[3. 身份验证](../stack/03-authentication.md) · [4. "
"计算资源](../stack/04-compute.md) · [6. 能力](../stack/06-capabilities.md) · [7. "
"记忆](../stack/07-memory.md) · [8. 权限](../stack/08-authority.md) · [9. "
"信任](../stack/09-trust.md) · [10. 治理](../stack/10-governance.md)"

