#: docs/providers/index.md:3
msgid ""
"A Birth Provider is any vendor, protocol, or self-hosted component that "
"hands an agent one of the things the [Birth Stack](../birth-stack.md) says "
"it needs: an inbox, a wallet, a sandbox, a secret store. The stack layers "
"are stable; the providers that fill them are not. This section exists so "
"that the churn stays in tables and the reasoning stays in prose."
msgstr ""
"诞生服务提供方（Birth Provider）是指为智能体提供[诞生栈](../birth-"
"stack.md)所需要素的任何供应商、协议或自托管组件：收件箱、钱包、沙箱、密钥存储。栈的层级是稳定的，填充这些层级的服务提供方则不然。设立本节的目的，是让变动留在表格中，而推理留在正文中。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:5
msgid "Requirement → capability → interface → provider"
msgstr "需求 → 能力 → 接口 → 服务提供方"

#: docs/providers/index.md:7
msgid ""
"Every provider chapter follows the same four-step derivation, introduced in "
"[From requirement to provider](../birth-stack.md#from-requirement-to-"
"provider):"
msgstr ""
"每个服务提供方章节都遵循相同的四步推导，该方法在[从需求到服务提供方](../birth-stack.md#from-requirement-to-"
"provider)中引入："

#: docs/providers/index.md:9
msgid ""
"**Birth requirement** — a sentence from a layer chapter: _the agent needs to"
" hold and spend value under a budget._"
msgstr "<strong>诞生需求</strong> — 来自某个层级章节的一句话：<em>智能体需要在预算约束下持有并支配价值。</em>"

#: docs/providers/index.md:10
msgid ""
"**Abstract capability** — the verbs, independent of any vendor: _hold keys, "
"sign transactions, enforce a spend policy, expose balances._"
msgstr "<strong>抽象能力</strong> — 与任何供应商无关的动词：<em>持有密钥、签署交易、执行支出策略、公开余额。</em>"

#: docs/providers/index.md:11
msgid ""
"**Provider interface** — the concrete technical surface a provider can "
"expose for those verbs: an SDK with a policy engine, a smart-account module,"
" a raw JSON-RPC signer."
msgstr ""
"<strong>服务提供方接口</strong> — 服务提供方可以为这些动词提供的具体技术界面：带策略引擎的 SDK、智能账户模块、原始 JSON-"
"RPC 签名器。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:12
msgid ""
"**Concrete providers** — the vendors and OSS projects that implement one or "
"more of those interfaces today."
msgstr "<strong>具体服务提供方</strong> — 当前实现了这些接口中一个或多个的供应商与开源项目。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:14
msgid ""
"The point of the middle two steps is portability. A Birth Profile that "
"records `spec.economy.wallets[].custody: mpc` and `provider: turnkey` can be"
" migrated to another MPC provider without rewriting the agent; one that "
"hard-codes a vendor SDK cannot. The [Migration](../lifecycle/migration.md) "
"chapter depends on this distinction."
msgstr ""
"中间两步的意义在于可移植性。记录了 `spec.economy.wallets[].custody: mpc` 和 `provider: "
"turnkey` 的诞生档案可以迁移到另一家 MPC 提供方而无需重写智能体；硬编码某个供应商 SDK "
"的档案则做不到。[迁移](../lifecycle/migration.md)章节依赖于这一区别。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:16
msgid ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart LR\n"
"    R[\"Requirement<br/><i>hold and spend value under a budget</i>\"] --> C[\"Capability<br/><i>custody keys · sign · enforce policy</i>\"]\n"
"    C --> I1[\"Interface: provider-held wallet + policy API\"]\n"
"    C --> I2[\"Interface: smart account + session keys\"]\n"
"    C --> I3[\"Interface: MPC / TEE signer\"]\n"
"    I1 --> P1[Coinbase CDP]\n"
"    I1 --> P2[Privy]\n"
"    I2 --> P3[Safe]\n"
"    I2 --> P4[ZeroDev]\n"
"    I3 --> P5[Turnkey]\n"
"    I3 --> P6[Lit Protocol]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart LR\n"
"    R[\"需求<br/><i>在预算约束下持有并支配价值</i>\"] --> C[\"能力<br/><i>托管密钥 · 签名 · 执行策略</i>\"]\n"
"    C --> I1[\"接口：提供方托管钱包 + 策略 API\"]\n"
"    C --> I2[\"接口：智能账户 + 会话密钥\"]\n"
"    C --> I3[\"接口：MPC / TEE 签名器\"]\n"
"    I1 --> P1[Coinbase CDP]\n"
"    I1 --> P2[Privy]\n"
"    I2 --> P3[Safe]\n"
"    I2 --> P4[ZeroDev]\n"
"    I3 --> P5[Turnkey]\n"
"    I3 --> P6[Lit Protocol]\n"
"```"

#: docs/providers/index.md:30
msgid ""
"The same shape holds for compute: _the agent needs somewhere to execute "
"untrusted code_ → _start, exec, snapshot, destroy an isolated environment_ →"
" _microVM API · container API · serverless sandbox SDK_ → E2B, Daytona, "
"Modal, Fly Machines, self-hosted Firecracker."
msgstr ""
"计算资源也遵循同样的模式：<em>智能体需要一个执行不可信代码的地方</em> → <em>启动、执行、快照、销毁隔离环境</em> → "
"<em>microVM API · 容器 API · 无服务器沙箱 SDK</em> → E2B、Daytona、Modal、Fly "
"Machines、自托管 Firecracker。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:32
msgid "Reading the tables"
msgstr "如何阅读这些表格"

#: docs/providers/index.md:34
msgid "Each chapter has one or two tables with a fixed column set:"
msgstr "每章包含一到两个具有固定列集的表格："

#: docs/providers/index.md:36
msgid "Column"
msgstr "列"

#: docs/providers/index.md:38
msgid "**Provider**"
msgstr "<strong>Provider（提供方）</strong>"

#: docs/providers/index.md:38
msgid ""
"Product or project name, linked to its official site or repository. Nothing "
"else is linked."
msgstr "产品或项目名称，链接到其官方网站或代码仓库。不链接其他任何内容。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:39
msgid "**Agent-native**"
msgstr "<strong>Agent-native（智能体原生）</strong>"

#: docs/providers/index.md:39
msgid ""
"`Yes` — the provider was built for, or has a dedicated product surface for, "
"non-human principals: agent-scoped inboxes, per-agent spend policies, "
"sandboxes that expect to be created and destroyed by code, MCP servers "
"maintained by the vendor. `Usable` — a general-purpose product with an API "
"good enough that an agent can be provisioned onto it, but the account model,"
" ToS, or onboarding still assume a human at the keyboard."
msgstr ""
"`Yes` —— "
"该提供方专为非人类主体构建，或拥有面向非人类主体的专属产品界面：智能体专属收件箱、按智能体划分的支出策略、预期由代码创建和销毁的沙箱、由供应商维护的 "
"MCP 服务器。`Usable` —— 通用产品，其 API 足以让智能体在其上完成开通，但账户模型、服务条款或注册流程仍假定键盘前坐着一个人。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:40
msgid "**OSS**"
msgstr "<strong>OSS（开源）</strong>"

#: docs/providers/index.md:40
msgid ""
"`Yes` if the core is open source under an OSI licence and can be self-"
"hosted; `No` otherwise; `Partial` if only SDKs or a reference implementation"
" are open."
msgstr "若核心在 OSI 许可证下开源且可自托管，则为 `Yes`；否则为 `No`；若仅 SDK 或参考实现开源，则为 `Partial`。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:41
msgid "**Pricing**"
msgstr "<strong>Pricing（定价）</strong>"

#: docs/providers/index.md:41
msgid ""
"One of `Free tier`, `Usage-based`, `Paid`, `OSS + cloud`, `n/a`. No numbers;"
" pricing pages move faster than this book."
msgstr ""
"取值为 `Free tier`、`Usage-based`、`Paid`、`OSS + cloud`、`n/a` "
"之一。不含具体数字；定价页面的变化速度快于本书。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:42
msgid "**Notes**"
msgstr "<strong>Notes（备注）</strong>"

#: docs/providers/index.md:42
msgid ""
"The one fact that decides whether this provider fits a given Birth Profile: "
"custody model, ToS constraint, region, interface."
msgstr "决定该提供方是否适配特定诞生档案的关键事实：托管模型、服务条款限制、地区、接口。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:44
msgid ""
"`Agent-native = Yes` is not an endorsement. A `Usable` provider with a "
"mature API is often the better choice; the column tells you how much of the "
"agent-specific work (policy, scoping, lifecycle) the provider does for you "
"and how much you carry yourself in layers [8](../stack/08-authority.md) and "
"[10](../stack/10-governance.md)."
msgstr ""
"`Agent-native = Yes` 并非背书。拥有成熟 API 的 `Usable` "
"提供方往往是更好的选择；该列告诉你提供方为你完成了多少智能体特有的工作（策略、作用域、生命周期），以及你自己在第 "
"[8](../stack/08-authority.md) 层和第 [10](../stack/10-governance.md) 层需要承担多少。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:46
msgid "Editorial rule"
msgstr "编辑规则"

#: docs/providers/index.md:48
msgid ""
"Links point only to the provider's own site, documentation, or repository, "
"or to a specification or RFC. No blog posts about a provider, no comparison "
"articles, no marketing adjectives (\"leading\", \"seamless\", \"enterprise-"
"grade\") in Notes. If a claim cannot be linked to an official page, it is "
"left out. Pull requests that add a provider must include the official URL "
"and fill every column."
msgstr ""
"链接仅指向提供方自己的网站、文档或代码仓库，或指向规范或 "
"RFC。备注中不允许出现关于提供方的博客文章、对比文章或营销形容词（“领先”“无缝”“企业级”）。如果某项说法无法链接到官方页面，则予以省略。添加提供方的"
" Pull Request 必须包含官方 URL 并填写所有列。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:50
msgid "The eleven provider chapters"
msgstr "十一个提供方章节"

#: docs/providers/index.md:52
msgid ""
"[Email](email.md) - Inboxes an agent can send from, receive into, and "
"complete signups with."
msgstr "[电子邮件](email.md) —— 智能体可用于发送、接收以及完成注册的收件箱。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:53
msgid ""
"[Phone, SMS & Voice](phone.md) - Numbers, OTP receipt, A2P messaging, and "
"voice; the hardest resource to obtain honestly."
msgstr "[电话、短信与语音](phone.md) —— 号码、OTP 接收、A2P 消息以及语音；最难以诚实方式获得的资源。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:54
msgid ""
"[Domains & DNS](domains.md) - Registrar and DNS APIs, `_well-known` and TXT "
"records, and why a subdomain of the owner's domain is the default."
msgstr ""
"[域名与 DNS](domains.md) - 注册商与 DNS API、`_well-known` 与 TXT "
"记录，以及为什么所有者域名的子域名是默认选择。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:55
msgid ""
"[Compute & Browsers](compute-and-browsers.md) - Sandboxes and runtimes where"
" agent code executes, and browsers it can drive."
msgstr "[计算资源与浏览器](compute-and-browsers.md) - 运行智能体代码的沙箱与运行时，以及它可以驱动的浏览器。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:56
msgid ""
"[Wallets & Keys](wallets.md) - Custody archetypes for on-chain keys: "
"provider-held with policy, MPC/TEE, smart accounts with session keys."
msgstr "[钱包与密钥](wallets.md) - 链上密钥的托管原型：带策略的服务方托管、MPC/TEE、带会话密钥的智能账户。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:57
msgid ""
"[Payments & Cards](payments-and-cards.md) - Fiat virtual cards, stablecoin "
"cards, and agent-payment rails; KYC/KYB is always passed by the owner."
msgstr "[支付与卡片](payments-and-cards.md) - 法币虚拟卡、稳定币卡与智能体支付通道；KYC/KYB 始终由所有者完成。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:58
msgid ""
"[Credentials & Tool Auth](credentials-and-tool-auth.md) - Token vaults, "
"identity providers with agent features, secret stores, and MCP gateways."
msgstr ""
"[凭证与工具身份验证](credentials-and-tool-auth.md) - 令牌保管库、具备智能体功能的身份提供方、密钥存储与 MCP "
"网关。"

#: docs/providers/index.md:59
msgid ""
"[Memory & Storage](memory-and-storage.md) - Memory layers, vector stores, "
"object storage, and the markdown-in-git pattern."
