#: docs/providers/domains.md:3
msgid ""
"A domain gives an agent a namespace it controls: an email address that is "
"not borrowed, a hostname for its endpoints, and a place to publish machine-"
"readable facts about itself (`/.well-known/agent-card.json`, `agents.txt`, "
"DKIM and SPF records, TXT-record proofs). In the "
"[Presence](../stack/02-presence.md) layer the domain is the root that email,"
" endpoints and much of [Trust](../stack/09-trust.md) hang from. An agent-"
"native domain provider is one where registration, renewal, nameserver "
"changes and every record type are reachable by API with scoped tokens, so "
"that the [Birth Procedure](../lifecycle/birth.md) can create "
"`agent.example.com`, add its MX and TXT records, and hand back a token that "
"can touch only that zone."
msgstr ""
"域名为智能体提供一个由其自身掌控的命名空间：一个非借用的电子邮件地址、其端点的主机名，以及一个发布关于自身的机器可读信息的位置（`/.well-"
"known/agent-card.json`、`agents.txt`、DKIM 和 SPF 记录、TXT "
"记录证明）。在[在线存在](../stack/02-presence.md)层中，域名是电子邮件、端点以及大部分[信任](../stack/09-trust.md)所依附的根基。智能体原生的域名服务提供方是指注册、续费、更改域名服务器以及所有记录类型都可通过"
" API 和范围受限令牌访问的提供方，从而使[诞生流程](../lifecycle/birth.md)能够创建 "
"`agent.example.com`、添加其 MX 和 TXT 记录，并交回一个只能操作该区域的令牌。"

#: docs/providers/domains.md:5
msgid ""
"The traps: registrars require a registrant with a legal name, postal address"
" and payment method, and ICANN's rules make the registrant of record the "
"accountable party, so the agent cannot be the registrant. Domain ownership "
"is a high-value credential; a token that can change nameservers can hijack "
"every email and endpoint under it. Most registrar APIs are broader than an "
"agent needs. For those reasons the default recommendation in this book is "
"that an agent gets a **subdomain of the owner's domain**, delegated by a DNS"
" token scoped to that zone, not its own registration. The owner keeps the "
"registrar account, the renewal, and the ability to unplug the agent with one"
" NS record. Only an agent that must outlive or be transferred independently "
"of its owner should hold its own name, and then usually through the owner's "
"legal entity anyway."
msgstr ""
"陷阱：注册商要求注册人提供法定姓名、邮政地址和支付方式，且 ICANN "
"规则将登记在册的注册人视为责任方，因此智能体不能成为注册人。域名所有权是一项高价值凭证；能够更改域名服务器的令牌可以劫持其下的所有电子邮件和端点。大多数注册商"
" API "
"的权限范围都比智能体所需的更广。基于这些原因，本书的默认建议是：智能体获得<strong>所有者域名的子域名，</strong>通过限定于该区域的 "
"DNS 令牌进行委托授权，而不是自行注册域名。所有者保留注册商账户、续费权，以及只需一条 NS "
"记录即可切断智能体的能力。只有必须比其所有者存续更久、或需独立于所有者转移的智能体，才应持有自己的域名，而且通常仍应通过所有者的法律实体持有。"

#: docs/providers/domains.md:9
msgid ""
"**Registrar API** - Availability check, registration, renewal, contact "
"update, nameserver update, transfer lock. Needed only if the agent registers"
" its own names."
msgstr ""
"<strong>注册商 API</strong> - 可用性查询、注册、续费、联系人更新、域名服务器更新、转移锁定。仅当智能体自行注册域名时才需要。"

#: docs/providers/domains.md:10
msgid ""
"**DNS zone API** - Create, read, update, delete records; the interface that "
"matters. Zone- or record-scoped tokens are the difference between a safe "
"delegation and a hijack risk."
msgstr ""
"<strong>DNS 区域 API</strong> - "
"创建、读取、更新、删除记录；这才是真正关键的接口。限定于区域或记录级别的令牌，是安全委托授权与劫持风险之间的分界线。"

#: docs/providers/domains.md:11
msgid ""
"**`_well-known` and TXT publication** - [RFC 8615](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc8615) well-known URIs for agent cards and discovery files;"
" TXT records for domain-ownership proofs demanded by email providers, OAuth "
"consoles and ACME DNS-01 challenges ([RFC 8555](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc8555))."
msgstr ""
"**`_well-known` 与 TXT 发布** - 用于智能体名片和发现文件的 [RFC 8615](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc8615) well-known URI；用于满足电子邮件提供商、OAuth 控制台和 ACME DNS-01 "
"质询（[RFC 8555](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8555)）所要求的域名所有权证明的 TXT 记录。"

#: docs/providers/domains.md:12
msgid ""
