msgid "The markdown-in-git pattern"
msgstr "git 中的 Markdown 模式"

#: docs/providers/memory-and-storage.md:37
msgid ""
"The lowest-tech option deserves a note because it solves several traps at "
"once. The agent keeps `memory/` as a directory of markdown files: one per "
"topic or entity, a daily log, and an index the agent loads at startup. "
"Writes are commits; the owner reviews the diff like any pull request, which "
"is the only memory system where poisoning is visible to a human before it "
"takes effect. Migration is `git clone`. Death is deleting the repo. It does "
"not scale to millions of facts or to semantic search without an index on "
"top, but for a single-owner agent it is often the right first store, with a "
"vector or graph layer added only when retrieval starts failing."
msgstr ""
"这个技术含量最低的方案值得一提，因为它一次性解决了多个陷阱。智能体将 `memory/` 维护为一个 Markdown "
"文件目录：每个主题或实体一个文件、一份每日日志，以及智能体启动时加载的索引。写入即提交；所有者像审阅任何拉取请求一样审阅差异，这是唯一一种在投毒生效前人类可见的记忆系统。迁移就是"
" `git "
"clone`。删除仓库即为终止。它无法扩展到数百万条事实，也不能在没有额外索引的情况下支持语义搜索，但对于单一所有者的智能体，它往往是合适的首选存储，只有当检索开始失效时才需要在其上添加向量或图层。"

