#: docs/providers/models-and-skills.md:3
msgid ""
"The [Capabilities](../stack/06-capabilities.md) layer is what the agent can "
"actually do: which models it can call, which tools it can invoke, and which "
"packaged procedures (skills) it knows how to follow. Provisioning it means "
"three things. First, model access through a gateway rather than a raw vendor"
" key, so that spend, rate and model choice are controlled per agent and the "
"vendor can be swapped. Second, a way to discover and install tools, which in"
" 2026 mostly means MCP servers found through a registry. Third, skills: "
"versioned folders of instructions and scripts the agent loads on demand, now"
" standardised as the Agent Skills format. Agent-native providers issue per-"
"agent keys with budgets, serve tools with machine-readable manifests, and "
"ship skills that any compliant client can load."
msgstr ""
"[能力](../stack/06-capabilities.md)层是智能体实际能做的事：它可以调用哪些模型、可以调用哪些工具，以及它知道如何遵循哪些打包的流程（技能）。对其进行供给意味着三件事。第一，通过网关而非原始厂商密钥访问模型，从而按智能体控制花费、速率和模型选择，并可更换厂商。第二，一种发现和安装工具的方式，在"
" 2026 年这主要指通过注册表找到的 MCP 服务器。第三，技能：智能体按需加载的带版本的指令和脚本文件夹，现已标准化为 Agent Skills "
"格式。面向智能体的原生服务提供方为每个智能体发放带预算的密钥、提供带机器可读清单的工具，并交付任何兼容客户端都能加载的技能。"

#: docs/providers/models-and-skills.md:5
msgid ""
"The traps: a shared vendor API key across agents means no per-agent budget, "
"no per-agent kill switch and no attribution in the audit log; tool "
"registries are a supply chain (OWASP ASI04) and a server's manifest is a "
"claim, not a proof, so pin versions and read the source; skills are "
"executable instructions and a malicious `SKILL.md` is a prompt injection "
"with a package manager; and model routers that silently fall back to a "
"different model change the agent's behaviour without anyone deciding to."
msgstr ""
"陷阱包括：多个智能体共享一个厂商 API "
"密钥意味着没有按智能体的预算、没有按智能体的紧急停止开关、审计日志中也无法归因；工具注册表是一条供应链（OWASP "
"ASI04），服务器的清单只是一种声明而非证明，因此要固定版本并阅读源码；技能是可执行指令，恶意的 `SKILL.md` "
"就是带包管理器的提示注入；而静默回退到其他模型的模型路由器会在无人决策的情况下改变智能体的行为。"

#: docs/providers/models-and-skills.md:9
msgid ""
"**OpenAI-compatible gateway** - One base URL and one virtual key per agent; "
"the gateway maps to any upstream vendor and enforces budgets, rate limits "
"and model allow-lists. The per-key budget is the cheapest "
"[Governance](../stack/10-governance.md) hook in the whole stack: set "
"`spec.governance.limits` at the gateway and the agent cannot overspend even "
"if its own code is compromised."
msgstr ""
"<strong>OpenAI 兼容网关</strong> - 每个智能体一个基础 URL "
"和一个虚拟密钥；网关映射到任意上游厂商并强制执行预算、速率限制和模型白名单。按密钥的预算是整个栈中最廉价的[治理](../stack/10-governance.md)抓手：在网关处设置"
" `spec.governance.limits`，即使智能体自身代码被攻破也无法超支。"

#: docs/providers/models-and-skills.md:10
msgid ""
"**Direct vendor API** - Anthropic, OpenAI, Google and others; needed for "
"features a gateway lags on, at the cost of managing keys and quotas per "
"vendor."
msgstr ""
"<strong>厂商直连 API</strong> - Anthropic、OpenAI、Google "
